&lt;th align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;dynamo-protocols&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;dynamo-parsers&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;dynamo-renderer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;dynamo-tokenizers&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;5.14.1&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;v5.4.0&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;v8.1.0&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;v5.1.0&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;v1.8.0&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Breaking Changes&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ACTION REQUIRED:&lt;/strong&gt; the following changes may require updates before upgrading. Entries are ordered by impact within each section.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Deprecated and Removed&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;KVBM (KV Block Manager) is deprecated in v1.5.0 and removal is targeted for v1.7.0; the &lt;code&gt;kvbm&lt;/code&gt; wheel and the vLLM KVBM launch and deploy examples ship unchanged for this release&lt;/strong&gt;.
&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Migrate:&lt;/strong&gt; Use the engine&#39;s native KV offloading for host and disk tiering. Cross-node KV cache sharing is the scope of the separate, early-stage KV Cache Runner (KVCR) project, which does not replace KVBM.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;CRD storage version promoted from v1alpha1 to v1beta1, with examples and Profiler output moving with it&lt;/strong&gt; (&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/11904&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/11904/hovercard&quot;&gt;#11904&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12375&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12375/hovercard&quot;&gt;#12375&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12506&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12506/hovercard&quot;&gt;#12506&lt;/a&gt;).
&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Migrate:&lt;/strong&gt; Upgrade the operator so the built-in CRD migrator converts stored objects.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;v1alpha1 admission webhook endpoints removed, and DGD and DCD validation served only at v1beta1 paths&lt;/strong&gt; (&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/11177&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/11177/hovercard&quot;&gt;#11177&lt;/a&gt;).
&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Migrate:&lt;/strong&gt; Update any custom Validating/MutatingWebhookConfiguration (not managed by the bundled Helm chart) to point at the v1beta1 DGD admission paths with apiVersions: [v1beta1].&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Go EPP removed, and the Rust EPP shipped inside the Frontend image is the default Endpoint Picker, with &lt;code&gt;eppConfig&lt;/code&gt; deprecated&lt;/strong&gt; (&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/11355&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/11355/hovercard&quot;&gt;#11355&lt;/a&gt;).
&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Migrate:&lt;/strong&gt; Update EPP deployment manifests and flags to the Rust EPP (LW-EPP) contract.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dynamo Snapshot moved to a standalone operator, removing the bundled chart, PodSnapshot CRDs, and reconciliation from Dynamo Operator&lt;/strong&gt; (&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13177&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13177/hovercard&quot;&gt;#13177&lt;/a&gt;).
&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Migrate:&lt;/strong&gt; Snapshot v0.1.0 now installs as its own operator from &lt;code&gt;oci://ghcr.io/ai-dynamo/snapshot/snapshot:0.1.0&lt;/code&gt;. For evaluation, the Dynamo platform chart can install it as a subchart with &lt;code&gt;global.snapshot.install=true&lt;/code&gt;, which is off by default. For production, install the Snapshot chart separately before upgrading Dynamo Operator, then set &lt;code&gt;checkpoint.enabled=true&lt;/code&gt; on the operator to turn checkpoint and restore back on.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;DynamoCheckpoint CRD, its Helm values, and &lt;code&gt;DYN_SNAPSHOT_RESTORE_STANDBY&lt;/code&gt; removed, and &lt;code&gt;checkpointRef&lt;/code&gt; now names a PodSnapshot&lt;/strong&gt; (&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14076&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14076/hovercard&quot;&gt;#14076&lt;/a&gt;).
&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Migrate:&lt;/strong&gt; Delete legacy DynamoCheckpoint resources, create PodSnapshot resources through the Snapshot operator, and point &lt;code&gt;checkpointRef&lt;/code&gt; at the PodSnapshot.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Unified-backend entry point and logits-processing adapters removed from the SGLang and vLLM workers&lt;/strong&gt; (&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12792&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12792/hovercard&quot;&gt;#12792&lt;/a&gt;).
&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Migrate:&lt;/strong&gt; Drop the unified-backend flag from SGLang/vLLM launch commands and use the standard worker invocation shown in the updated CLI templates.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AIConfigurator renamed to AISimulate: aiconfigurator wheels replaced by the &lt;code&gt;aisimulate&lt;/code&gt; package, and the &lt;code&gt;python -m dynamo.replay&lt;/code&gt; CLI removed&lt;/strong&gt; (&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13665&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13665/hovercard&quot;&gt;#13665&lt;/a&gt;).
&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Migrate:&lt;/strong&gt; Install the consolidated &lt;code&gt;aisimulate&lt;/code&gt; wheel/&lt;code&gt;aisimulate-core&lt;/code&gt; crate instead of the separate &lt;code&gt;aiconfigurator&lt;/code&gt; packages (compatibility import namespaces ship inside the AISimulate wheel).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Planner performance-model and Mocker engine bindings removed from &lt;code&gt;dynamo._core&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; (&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12454&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12454/hovercard&quot;&gt;#12454&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12446&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12446/hovercard&quot;&gt;#12446&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12525&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12525/hovercard&quot;&gt;#12525&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Offline replay API returns a single &lt;code&gt;ReplayReport&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;--report-jsonl&lt;/code&gt; renamed to &lt;code&gt;--per-request-jsonl&lt;/code&gt;, and per-request capture is opt-in&lt;/strong&gt; (&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12363&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12363/hovercard&quot;&gt;#12363&lt;/a&gt;).
&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Migrate:&lt;/strong&gt; Update replay invocations/scripts to pass &lt;code&gt;--per-request-jsonl&lt;/code&gt; instead of &lt;code&gt;--report-jsonl&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SGLang &lt;code&gt;call_tokenizer_manager&lt;/code&gt; passthrough route and &lt;code&gt;RLMixin&lt;/code&gt; export removed&lt;/strong&gt; (&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12246&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12246/hovercard&quot;&gt;#12246&lt;/a&gt;).
&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Migrate:&lt;/strong&gt; Declare each needed tokenizer-manager or engine method explicitly with &lt;code&gt;--engine-route&lt;/code&gt; (or &lt;code&gt;DYN_SGLANG_ENGINE_ROUTES&lt;/code&gt;) and call the configured &lt;code&gt;/engine/&amp;lt;path&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt; instead of the generic &lt;code&gt;call_tokenizer_manager&lt;/code&gt; endpoint.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PodSnapshot capture target now comes from the required &lt;code&gt;PodReference.Containers&lt;/code&gt; field instead of a pod annotation&lt;/strong&gt; (&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12068&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12068/hovercard&quot;&gt;#12068&lt;/a&gt;).
&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Migrate:&lt;/strong&gt; Update the PodSnapshot/PodSnapshotContent CRDs and add exactly one entry to spec.source.podRef.containers in any hand-authored manifests, otherwise admission rejects them.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;GMS Snapshot feature gate removed, and IntraPod Snapshot enabled by default under the Checkpoint gate and unsupported combinations rejected&lt;/strong&gt; (&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12685&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12685/hovercard&quot;&gt;#12685&lt;/a&gt;).
&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Migrate:&lt;/strong&gt; Remove the GMS Snapshot feature-gate setting from your operator Helm values/args.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Automatic tokenizer fallback to Hugging Face is deprecated and will stop being the default&lt;/strong&gt; (&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12923&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12923/hovercard&quot;&gt;#12923&lt;/a&gt;).
&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Migrate:&lt;/strong&gt; Set --no-tokenizer-fallback or DYN_TOKENIZER_FALLBACK=false to adopt the future behavior now, and ensure your model&#39;s tokenizer.json is supported by the selected backend.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Removed &lt;code&gt;nsRestorePath&lt;/code&gt; snapshot config/Helm value&lt;/strong&gt; (&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12626&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12626/hovercard&quot;&gt;#12626&lt;/a&gt;).
&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Migrate:&lt;/strong&gt; Delete any &lt;code&gt;nsRestorePath&lt;/code&gt; setting from snapshot chart values/config.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Shared AWS EFA Kustomize components removed in favor of instance-type template selections&lt;/strong&gt; (&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13125&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13125/hovercard&quot;&gt;#13125&lt;/a&gt;).
&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Migrate:&lt;/strong&gt; Update overlays that referenced the aws-efa-p8d8/p8d16/p16d16 shared Components to select the new instance-type template (e.g. templates/aws-efa/p5.48xlarge) or the local components/efa Component.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Legacy Nemotron-3-Ultra Day-0 recipe manifests replaced by Refresh profile paths without the &lt;code&gt;nvcr-secret&lt;/code&gt; imagePullSecret&lt;/strong&gt; (&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13226&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13226/hovercard&quot;&gt;#13226&lt;/a&gt;).
&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Migrate:&lt;/strong&gt; Update any references/automation pointing at the old Day-0 recipe directories to the corresponding new Refresh profile paths (SKU + context + serving shape).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qwen3.8-2.4T-A95B recipe renamed with an &lt;code&gt;-fp8&lt;/code&gt; suffix, changing the served model name and weight cache key&lt;/strong&gt; (&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13265&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13265/hovercard&quot;&gt;#13265&lt;/a&gt;).
&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Migrate:&lt;/strong&gt; Re-run the model-download Job to fetch Qwen/Qwen3.8-2.4T-A95B-FP8 and update any client requests to use the new served model name.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;DeepSeek-V4 model-download manifest split and renamed, and the default downloaded checkpoint is now FP8&lt;/strong&gt; (&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13034&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13034/hovercard&quot;&gt;#13034&lt;/a&gt;).
&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Migrate:&lt;/strong&gt; Apply the SKU-specific manifest (model-download-fp8.yaml for H200/most variants, model-download-nvfp4.yaml for B200 agentic variants) instead of the removed model-download.yaml, and update any references to the old Job name.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Notable Behavioral Changes&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Guided tool calls stream incrementally by default instead of a single terminal chunk&lt;/strong&gt; (&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12576&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12576/hovercard&quot;&gt;#12576&lt;/a&gt;).
&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Migrate:&lt;/strong&gt; Clients that assumed a single complete tool-call chunk must accumulate incremental tool-call argument deltas, or set DYN_ENABLE_GUIDED_TOOL_STREAMING=0 to restore buffering.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Over-context requests rejected before streaming, and an omitted &lt;code&gt;max_tokens&lt;/code&gt; now derives from the engine-published TokenBudget&lt;/strong&gt; (&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12092&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12092/hovercard&quot;&gt;#12092&lt;/a&gt;).
&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Migrate:&lt;/strong&gt; Update clients and retry/monitoring logic to handle a non-200 HTTP client error for over-context requests instead of an inline streamed error.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Thinking/reasoning controls resolved once with new precedence and written to all three template keys&lt;/strong&gt; (&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/11739&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/11739/hovercard&quot;&gt;#11739&lt;/a&gt;).
&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Migrate:&lt;/strong&gt; If you relied on the previous per-backend resolution or on only &lt;code&gt;enable_thinking&lt;/code&gt; being set, drop manual chat_template_args thinking overrides and rely on the documented precedence order.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Gemma 4 reasoning parsing now requires explicit enable_thinking=true&lt;/strong&gt; (&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13061&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13061/hovercard&quot;&gt;#13061&lt;/a&gt;).
&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Migrate:&lt;/strong&gt; Set &lt;code&gt;chat_template_args: {&quot;enable_thinking&quot;: true}&lt;/code&gt; in requests to Gemma 4 models to keep receiving parsed reasoning_content.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Embedding tokenization adds special tokens by default and moves to the worker, with Frontend tokenization opt-in&lt;/strong&gt; (&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12157&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12157/hovercard&quot;&gt;#12157&lt;/a&gt;).
&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Migrate:&lt;/strong&gt; Set &lt;code&gt;add_special_tokens: false&lt;/code&gt; on embedding requests or export DYN_EMBEDDING_TOKENIZATION_ADD_SPECIAL_TOKENS=false to keep the previous tokenization behavior.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;vLLM encode worker embedding cache now disabled by default (gated on --multimodal-embedding-cache-capacity-gb)&lt;/strong&gt; (&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14452&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14452/hovercard&quot;&gt;#14452&lt;/a&gt;).
&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Migrate:&lt;/strong&gt; Set --multimodal-embedding-cache-capacity-gb to a positive value to keep embedding caching in the vLLM encode worker.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;DGD, DCD, and DGDR admission requires a main container image, and a non-semver image tag (digest, custom build tag, or &lt;code&gt;:latest&lt;/code&gt;) requires &lt;code&gt;runtimeVersionOverride&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; (&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/10494&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/10494/hovercard&quot;&gt;#10494&lt;/a&gt;).
&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Migrate:&lt;/strong&gt; Set the main container image on every component (&lt;code&gt;spec.components[*].podTemplate.spec.containers[name=main].image&lt;/code&gt; in v1beta1, &lt;code&gt;spec.services.&amp;lt;name&amp;gt;.extraPodSpec.mainContainer.image&lt;/code&gt; in v1alpha1) and add &lt;code&gt;runtimeVersionOverride: &quot;&amp;lt;X.Y.Z&amp;gt;&quot;&lt;/code&gt; wherever the image tag is not a semantic version, including a DGDR whose &lt;code&gt;spec.image&lt;/code&gt; is not. The checks are ratcheted: an unchanged existing component stays admissible, but adding or changing an image applies them, so set the override in the same update that changes the tag. Full details are in the &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/blob/release/1.5.0/deploy/helm/charts/platform/README.md#-upgrading-notes&quot;&gt;platform chart upgrading notes&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;runtimeVersionOverride now participates in worker hash and can trigger rollouts&lt;/strong&gt; (&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12633&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12633/hovercard&quot;&gt;#12633&lt;/a&gt;).
&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Migrate:&lt;/strong&gt; Before upgrading, ensure runtimeVersionOverride matches the image&#39;s actual runtime version and expect a one-time worker rollout when the resolved version (&amp;gt;=1.5.0) changes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Worker canary health checks enabled by default in operator-rendered pods&lt;/strong&gt; (&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/11083&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/11083/hovercard&quot;&gt;#11083&lt;/a&gt;).
&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Migrate:&lt;/strong&gt; Set DYN_HEALTH_CHECK_ENABLED=false explicitly in the worker container env if you need the previous behavior.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Worker liveness probe failureThreshold default raised from 1 to 3 for runtime &amp;gt;= 1.5.0&lt;/strong&gt; (&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13512&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13512/hovercard&quot;&gt;#13512&lt;/a&gt;).
&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Migrate:&lt;/strong&gt; No action needed unless you rely on immediate restart on first liveness failure.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;code&gt;nvidia.com/workload-provider&lt;/code&gt; is persisted and immutable, with no fallback to the Component provider when Grove is unavailable&lt;/strong&gt; (&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12942&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12942/hovercard&quot;&gt;#12942&lt;/a&gt;).
&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Migrate:&lt;/strong&gt; To change the workload provider of an existing DynamoGraphDeployment, delete and recreate the DGD instead of toggling nvidia.com/enable-grove or the Grove feature gate.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Elastic-EP components require an explicit container command, and single-pod components start a Ray head and inject &lt;code&gt;POD_IP&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;VLLM_DP_M*&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; (&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12943&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12943/hovercard&quot;&gt;#12943&lt;/a&gt;).
&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Migrate:&lt;/strong&gt; If you set --enable-elastic-ep on a single-pod component and relied on it being a no-op, remove the flag.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;componentType/type fields are now immutable after being set&lt;/strong&gt; (&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13763&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13763/hovercard&quot;&gt;#13763&lt;/a&gt;).
&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Migrate:&lt;/strong&gt; Delete and recreate the DynamoComponentDeployment/DynamoGraphDeployment (or component) instead of editing its componentType/type field in place.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;vLLM STORAGE KV events now indexed on the Disk tier, and REMOTE or unknown-locality events dropped&lt;/strong&gt; (&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/11571&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/11571/hovercard&quot;&gt;#11571&lt;/a&gt;).
&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Migrate:&lt;/strong&gt; Expect STORAGE offload prefixes to be scored via the Disk tier and non-local (REMOTE/unknown locality) KV events to be ignored.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;code&gt;DYN_USE_KV_EVENTS&lt;/code&gt; renamed to &lt;code&gt;DYN_ROUTER_USE_KV_EVENTS&lt;/code&gt; (alias kept), and previously ignored &lt;code&gt;DYN_*&lt;/code&gt; Router env vars now honored&lt;/strong&gt; (&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13840&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13840/hovercard&quot;&gt;#13840&lt;/a&gt;).
&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Migrate:&lt;/strong&gt; Switch to DYN_ROUTER_USE_KV_EVENTS.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;DYN_RUNTIME_NUM_WORKER_THREADS / DYN_RUNTIME_MAX_BLOCKING_THREADS now actually apply to the runtime serving traffic&lt;/strong&gt; (&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13849&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13849/hovercard&quot;&gt;#13849&lt;/a&gt;).
&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Migrate:&lt;/strong&gt; Re-check any explicit DYN_RUNTIME_NUM_WORKER_THREADS / DYN_RUNTIME_MAX_BLOCKING_THREADS values (and unset ones relying on the old per-CPU/512 sizing) since they now change frontend thread counts and concurrency.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;EPP replica sync validates &lt;code&gt;POD_IP&lt;/code&gt; at config-parse time and no longer resolves the port from the &lt;code&gt;replica-agg&lt;/code&gt; Service port&lt;/strong&gt; (&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13811&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13811/hovercard&quot;&gt;#13811&lt;/a&gt;).
&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Migrate:&lt;/strong&gt; Ensure every EPP replica binds the same replica-sync port (9092 by default) and set DYN_EPP_REPLICA_SYNC_PORT if your existing &lt;code&gt;replica-agg&lt;/code&gt; targetPort differed.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Standalone router --endpoint namespace now overridden by DYN_NAMESPACE / worker suffix&lt;/strong&gt; (&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12160&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12160/hovercard&quot;&gt;#12160&lt;/a&gt;).
&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Migrate:&lt;/strong&gt; If you relied on the namespace embedded in --endpoint, unset/align DYN_NAMESPACE and DYN_NAMESPACE_WORKER_SUFFIX so the router resolves workers in the intended namespace.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Unsupported tool_call_parser names now rejected at model registration&lt;/strong&gt; (&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13828&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13828/hovercard&quot;&gt;#13828&lt;/a&gt;).
&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Migrate:&lt;/strong&gt; Set --tool-call-parser (or tool_call_parser in runtime config) to one of the parser names listed in the new validation error message before upgrading.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;tool_call arguments auto-normalized to JSON object for glm47 tool_call_parser&lt;/strong&gt; (&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12332&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12332/hovercard&quot;&gt;#12332&lt;/a&gt;).
&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Migrate:&lt;/strong&gt; If you rely on the raw JSON-string form of historical tool_call arguments with the glm47 tool_call_parser, explicitly set tool_call_arguments_format: json_string in the model runtime config.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Snapshot saver/loader CLI without --device now fans out to all visible GPUs&lt;/strong&gt; (&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13301&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13301/hovercard&quot;&gt;#13301&lt;/a&gt;).
&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Migrate:&lt;/strong&gt; Pass an explicit --device N to retain single-process behavior.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Planner Prometheus requests now time out after 10s and no longer retry&lt;/strong&gt; (&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13245&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13245/hovercard&quot;&gt;#13245&lt;/a&gt;).
&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Migrate:&lt;/strong&gt; If your Prometheus endpoint is slow, raise the limit via DYN_PLANNER_PROMETHEUS_REQUEST_TIMEOUT_SECONDS or metric_pulling_prometheus_request_timeout_seconds, and expect failed queries to no longer be retried within a collection cycle.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Profiler-generated vLLM worker args no longer pin --max-model-len, and naive fallback now sizes from declared workload isl/osl&lt;/strong&gt; (&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14205&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14205/hovercard&quot;&gt;#14205&lt;/a&gt;).
&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Migrate:&lt;/strong&gt; Re-run the profiler and, if a specific context length is required, set --max-model-len explicitly via DGD overrides since the generated config no longer pins it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;JPEG decoding switches to libjpeg-turbo by default when libturbojpeg is present&lt;/strong&gt; (&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/11157&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/11157/hovercard&quot;&gt;#11157&lt;/a&gt;).
&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Migrate:&lt;/strong&gt; Set DYN_MM_ENABLE_LIBJPEG=0 to keep the previous pure-Rust image::ImageReader JPEG decode path (pixel output may differ slightly from TurboJPEG).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Features &amp;amp; Improvements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Frontend &amp;amp; Agents&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Native Kimi K3 Processing:&lt;/strong&gt; Added native Kimi K3 rendering, parsing, and tokenization to the frontend, covering thinking, XTML tool calls, and response wrappers. Fixed the SGLang chat processor to split K3 reasoning content and strip the terminal &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;|end_of_msg|&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt; token (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5013925178&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/12396&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12396/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12396&quot;&gt;#12396&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5013925175&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/12395&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12395/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12395&quot;&gt;#12395&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pluggable Tokenizer Backend Selection:&lt;/strong&gt; Added the Baseten tokenizer as a selectable frontend backend via &lt;code&gt;--tokenizer basetenkenizer&lt;/code&gt; or &lt;code&gt;DYN_TOKENIZER=basetenkenizer&lt;/code&gt;, and made the Hugging Face fallback policy configurable so a failed load no longer silently serves Hugging Face instead (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5012591810&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/12376&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12376/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12376&quot;&gt;#12376&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5107243856&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/12923&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12923/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12923&quot;&gt;#12923&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;OpenAI API &amp;amp; Validation&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Assistant Message Continuation Support:&lt;/strong&gt; Added support for &lt;code&gt;add_generation_prompt&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;continue_final_message&lt;/code&gt; in the chat preprocessor, which previously ignored both. Continuation requires &lt;code&gt;add_generation_prompt&lt;/code&gt; set explicitly to false, since it defaults to true and the two flags together are rejected; the final message may be from any role, and prompts truncate to match Hugging Face &lt;code&gt;apply_chat_template&lt;/code&gt; (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5259302009&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13841&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13841/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13841&quot;&gt;#13841&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responses API Correctness Fixes:&lt;/strong&gt; Fixed streamed backend error propagation, tool-call and reasoning ordering, and &lt;code&gt;parallel_tool_calls&lt;/code&gt; handling, added &lt;code&gt;chat_template_args&lt;/code&gt; support, and added &lt;code&gt;POST /v1/responses/input_tokens&lt;/code&gt; for estimated input token counts (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5024220874&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/12442&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12442/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12442&quot;&gt;#12442&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5024965777&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/12462&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12462/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12462&quot;&gt;#12462&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5170785417&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13367&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13367/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13367&quot;&gt;#13367&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5210018391&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13624&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13624/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13624&quot;&gt;#13624&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5247973238&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13768&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13768/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13768&quot;&gt;#13768&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Exact Multimodal Generate Routing:&lt;/strong&gt; Added routing-only token projection for &lt;code&gt;/inference/v1/generate&lt;/code&gt; so image identity feeds KV cache-aware routing without changing execution tokens, and made engine, block size, and LoRA selection atomic per &lt;code&gt;WorkerSet&lt;/code&gt;. Malformed placeholders fall back to token-only routing (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;4870265551&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/11588&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/11588/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/11588&quot;&gt;#11588&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Opt-In SSE Keep-Alive:&lt;/strong&gt; Added the &lt;code&gt;DYN_HTTP_SSE_KEEP_ALIVE_INTERVAL_MS&lt;/code&gt; environment variable to emit spec-compliant Server-Sent Events (SSE) comment frames during idle streams. Unset, zero, or invalid values keep keep-alive disabled, so the default behavior is unchanged for clients that do not ignore comment frames (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5024683831&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/12453&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12453/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12453&quot;&gt;#12453&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Guided Decoding &amp;amp; Tool Calling&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;V2 Unified Tool-Call Parser:&lt;/strong&gt; Streamed guided tool calls by default, routed Qwen3 through the v2 unified parser so reasoning stays after tool calls, and served Muse-Glimmer-30B default-on through the same parser, adding &lt;code&gt;--dyn-tool-call-parser muse_glimmer&lt;/code&gt; (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5052173675&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/12576&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12576/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12576&quot;&gt;#12576&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5166716365&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13340&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13340/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13340&quot;&gt;#13340&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Reasoning &amp;amp; Thinking Controls&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Deployment-Level Thinking Controls:&lt;/strong&gt; Added a deployment-level default thinking mode applied at chat-template rendering, with request-level overrides still taking priority, plus fixes for MiniMax M3&#39;s &lt;code&gt;thinking_mode&lt;/code&gt; default and Gemma 4 reasoning parsing gated on explicit &lt;code&gt;enable_thinking&lt;/code&gt; (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;4770061406&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/11047&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/11047/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/11047&quot;&gt;#11047&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;4897108181&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/11739&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/11739/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/11739&quot;&gt;#11739&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5067420941&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/12687&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12687/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12687&quot;&gt;#12687&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5125719985&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13061&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13061/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13061&quot;&gt;#13061&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Configurable Reasoning Output Field:&lt;/strong&gt; Added the &lt;code&gt;DYN_REASONING_FIELD_NAME&lt;/code&gt; environment variable to select whether chat completion responses carry reasoning content in the &lt;code&gt;reasoning&lt;/code&gt; or &lt;code&gt;reasoning_content&lt;/code&gt; field, defaulting to &lt;code&gt;reasoning_content&lt;/code&gt;. Routed both streaming and non-streaming emit sites through the new selection so reasoning-only chunks are no longer dropped (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;4843451186&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/11464&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/11464/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/11464&quot;&gt;#11464&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Tokenizers &amp;amp; Model Processing&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Single-Flush Detokenization Metrics:&lt;/strong&gt; Changed the frontend to publish detokenization Prometheus counters once per stream instead of per chunk, removing cumulative overcounting while still recording partial metrics for cancellations, errors, timeouts, and early drops (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5116856245&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/12999&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12999/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12999&quot;&gt;#12999&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Agents &amp;amp; Request Classification&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Agent Request Trigger Classification:&lt;/strong&gt; Added an &lt;code&gt;AgentContext.input_trigger&lt;/code&gt; field classifying incoming agent requests as &lt;code&gt;user_message&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;tool_result&lt;/code&gt;, or &lt;code&gt;other&lt;/code&gt; across OpenAI and Anthropic APIs, extended to Responses tool-output variants, and carried Codex compaction and thread-lineage metadata into agent context (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5085372888&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/12787&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12787/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12787&quot;&gt;#12787&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5254850916&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13819&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13819/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13819&quot;&gt;#13819&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5118024506&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13012&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13012/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13012&quot;&gt;#13012&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5004045278&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/12331&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12331/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12331&quot;&gt;#12331&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Scheduling&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Two-Tier Cost Worker Selection Policy:&lt;/strong&gt; Added &lt;code&gt;dynamo-two-tier-cost-fn&lt;/code&gt; as a built-in worker-selection policy that ranks workers on active-request load first and device-KV prefix overlap second, and enabled &lt;code&gt;custom-policy&lt;/code&gt; by default so a stock build selects it from YAML with no rebuild (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5392511470&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14498&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14498/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14498&quot;&gt;#14498&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Custom Worker-Selection Policy Catalog:&lt;/strong&gt; Added native &lt;code&gt;WorkerScorer&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;WorkerPicker&lt;/code&gt; policies through the built-in selection path, with a &lt;code&gt;worker_selection&lt;/code&gt; YAML catalog for the KV frontend and selection services. Routed built-in strategies through one &lt;code&gt;WorkerSelector::select_worker&lt;/code&gt; entry point (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5034612366&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/12526&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12526/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12526&quot;&gt;#12526&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5039130201&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/12536&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12536/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12536&quot;&gt;#12536&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5188318109&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13513&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13513/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13513&quot;&gt;#13513&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5098656392&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/12891&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12891/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12891&quot;&gt;#12891&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5053361056&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/12585&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12585/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12585&quot;&gt;#12585&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pluggable Worker Selection Filters:&lt;/strong&gt; Added composable &lt;code&gt;WorkerFilter&lt;/code&gt; policies to custom worker selection, running eligibility first and filters before scorers and the picker, returning HTTP 503 when filters reject every eligible worker, plus a &lt;code&gt;min_effective_overlap_blocks&lt;/code&gt; cache-affinity example (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5099837009&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/12897&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12897/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12897&quot;&gt;#12897&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5099755492&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/12896&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12896/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12896&quot;&gt;#12896&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dynamic Worker Taint Updates:&lt;/strong&gt; Added an &lt;code&gt;update_model_taints&lt;/code&gt; Python API and &lt;code&gt;POST /engine/update/model_taints&lt;/code&gt; route across SGLang, TensorRT-LLM, and vLLM worker modes, so base-model routing metadata can change at runtime without restarting workers, waking pending scheduler requests (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5055812066&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/12620&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12620/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12620&quot;&gt;#12620&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Tiered KV Event Ingestion:&lt;/strong&gt; Added an event-driven Mooncake shared-cache index for SGLang HiCache and routed vLLM native-storage KV events to Dynamo Router&#39;s Disk tier with a fail-closed locality policy. Hardened event conversion to fail closed on unrecognized KV event media (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;4820552763&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/11239&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/11239/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/11239&quot;&gt;#11239&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;4861499263&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/11571&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/11571/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/11571&quot;&gt;#11571&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5024752840&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/12456&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12456/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12456&quot;&gt;#12456&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Remote KV Reuse Hints:&lt;/strong&gt; Added an experimental router-generated &lt;code&gt;router_hint&lt;/code&gt; for backend requests when Dynamo Router finds a better non-target source prefix, a signal that remote KV fetchers such as the early-stage KV Cache Runner (KVCR) can use to pull KV blocks from a peer. Carried router-hint and worker-role metadata through vLLM attachment intents, and preserved KV source-health warnings across endpoint rebinds (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;4888211552&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/11695&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/11695/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/11695&quot;&gt;#11695&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5237785102&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13725&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13725/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13725&quot;&gt;#13725&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5113260725&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/12959&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12959/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12959&quot;&gt;#12959&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Conditional Disaggregation Bypass Orchestration:&lt;/strong&gt; Added Router orchestration of the conditional disaggregation bypass path (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;4895289209&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/11725&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/11725/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/11725&quot;&gt;#11725&lt;/a&gt;), with the bypass behavior exposed through Router configuration (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;4895174499&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/11723&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/11723/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/11723&quot;&gt;#11723&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Planner Minimum Endpoint Floors:&lt;/strong&gt; Added runtime-configurable &lt;code&gt;prefill_min_endpoint&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;decode_min_endpoint&lt;/code&gt;, and &lt;code&gt;min_endpoint&lt;/code&gt; settings with a loopback-only &lt;code&gt;GET/PATCH /v1/min-endpoints&lt;/code&gt; API, enforced across scaling and budgets, and fixed SLA-driven scaling that left deployments below the configured minimum during a metrics outage (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5123600842&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13038&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13038/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13038&quot;&gt;#13038&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5406395164&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14575&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14575/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14575&quot;&gt;#14575&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Power-Aware Planner Scaling:&lt;/strong&gt; Added Kubernetes-only power-aware scaling where per-GPU caps set through &lt;code&gt;dynamo.nvidia.com/gpu-power-limit&lt;/code&gt; annotations are enforced by the Power Agent, and the Planner clamps scaling proposals against &lt;code&gt;total_gpu_power_limit&lt;/code&gt; without needing Pod write access (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;4950012888&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/12012&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12012/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12012&quot;&gt;#12012&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;KV Event Ingestion &amp;amp; Tiering&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Capacity-Bounded Approximate LRU:&lt;/strong&gt; Added an experimental, opt-in capacity-bounded LRU eviction policy for Dynamo Router&#39;s local approximate primary indexer, configurable through the CLI, environment variables, and the Python and Rust APIs. Each request lease is released on completion, abort, cancellation, or failure (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5229345819&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13701&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13701/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13701&quot;&gt;#13701&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Multimodal KV Event Normalization:&lt;/strong&gt; Normalized vLLM image and video object hashes to frontend-compatible pad values on the worker side, including mixed boundary blocks. Propagated an optional &lt;code&gt;video_token_id&lt;/code&gt; through the KV-event publisher paths, falling back to native vLLM behavior when mapping is ambiguous (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5269952714&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13910&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13910/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13910&quot;&gt;#13910&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Parallelized Brokered ZMQ Ingress:&lt;/strong&gt; Reworked the KV Router broker subscriber to poll broker SUB sockets and dispatch batches to bounded per-publisher lanes instead of a lossy shared broadcast channel. A slow publisher no longer blocks the shared reader (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5320017116&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14167&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14167/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14167&quot;&gt;#14167&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Multi-DC Relay &amp;amp; Remote KV Hints&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;KV DC Relay Contract Alignment:&lt;/strong&gt; Indexed canonical Dynamo sequence hashes in the DC exact-state cuckoo filter instead of engine-specific hashes, and aligned the &lt;code&gt;VllmResidencyV1&lt;/code&gt; raw-event contract on ownership. Added a transport-neutral &lt;code&gt;RelayPublicationSource&lt;/code&gt; interface decoupling publication drivers from gRPC and protobuf (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5184286974&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13471&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13471/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13471&quot;&gt;#13471&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5187997337&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13510&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13510/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13510&quot;&gt;#13510&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5298685155&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14041&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14041/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14041&quot;&gt;#14041&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Relay Serving Topology Derivation:&lt;/strong&gt; Added per-namespace model readiness, pool query semantics, and per-worker load observations to the KV DC Relay, derived from deployment cards and the &lt;code&gt;ActiveLoad&lt;/code&gt; stream. All facts are consumable in-process through watch and snapshot handles on &lt;code&gt;KvDcRelay&lt;/code&gt; (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5192468570&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13539&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13539/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13539&quot;&gt;#13539&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Router Configuration &amp;amp; State&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Worker-Advertised Router Configuration:&lt;/strong&gt; Exposed router flags on workers so a worker set declares its own routing strategy in its model deployment card, reachable from SGLang, TensorRT-LLM, and vLLM. Applied it to the prefill hop, which previously inherited the decode set&#39;s mode (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5144745588&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13192&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13192/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13192&quot;&gt;#13192&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5145374804&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13197&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13197/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13197&quot;&gt;#13197&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Hard and Soft Session Affinity:&lt;/strong&gt; Added a &lt;code&gt;--router-session-affinity-mode hard|soft&lt;/code&gt; flag and &lt;code&gt;DYN_ROUTER_SESSION_AFFINITY_MODE&lt;/code&gt; variable, with &lt;code&gt;hard&lt;/code&gt; as the default. In soft mode the stored session target passes through selection as an affinity target custom policies can override (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5269169796&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13907&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13907/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13907&quot;&gt;#13907&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Planner &amp;amp; Profiler&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Profiler DGD v1beta1 Migration:&lt;/strong&gt; Moved profiler-generated DynamoGraphDeployment resources to the native &lt;code&gt;nvidia.com/v1beta1&lt;/code&gt; &lt;code&gt;spec.components&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;podTemplate&lt;/code&gt; schema, with packaged v1beta1 blueprints for SGLang, TensorRT-LLM, vLLM, and Mocker so profiler behavior no longer depends on public example manifests. Explicitly versioned v1alpha1 DGD overrides remain supported while generated deployments emit v1beta1 (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5033341517&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/12506&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12506/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12506&quot;&gt;#12506&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Kubernetes Deployment&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;llm-d Batch Gateway Integration:&lt;/strong&gt; Added an experimental llm-d Batch Gateway example for offline inference covering the OpenAI Batch API file and job lifecycle. Gated asynchronous dispatch on frontend model readiness, failing closed with a zero budget when the metric is absent (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5085221338&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/12784&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12784/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12784&quot;&gt;#12784&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5281440584&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13978&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13978/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13978&quot;&gt;#13978&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Runtime Version Override Field:&lt;/strong&gt; Added &lt;code&gt;runtimeVersionOverride&lt;/code&gt; to DGD, DCD, and DGDR specs as an explicit runtime-compatibility declaration when an image tag lacks one. Included the resolved version in the v2 worker hash so an override matches its equivalent image tag (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;4623269511&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/10494&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/10494/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/10494&quot;&gt;#10494&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5062482377&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/12633&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12633/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12633&quot;&gt;#12633&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Runtime Feature Gates:&lt;/strong&gt; Added per-feature runtime gates in the Operator whose rendered defaults depend only on the resolved Dynamo runtime compatibility version, including a &lt;code&gt;CanaryHealthChecks&lt;/code&gt; gate introduced by Dynamo runtime v1.4.0 and normalized runtime-version comparison. Rendering stays stable across operator-only upgrades, and explicit user configuration remains authoritative (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5017816229&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/12421&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12421/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12421&quot;&gt;#12421&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Standalone Snapshot CRD Migration:&lt;/strong&gt; Migrated checkpoint capture and restore to standalone Snapshot resources, replacing DGD-managed DynamoCheckpoint, moved the capture target to a first-class &lt;code&gt;PodReference.Containers&lt;/code&gt; field, and switched restore-compatibility identity to a SHA-256 fingerprint (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5304676661&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14076&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14076/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14076&quot;&gt;#14076&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;4956791562&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/12068&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12068/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12068&quot;&gt;#12068&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5425601248&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14724&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14724/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14724&quot;&gt;#14724&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5180049683&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13448&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13448/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13448&quot;&gt;#13448&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5180782231&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13452&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13452/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13452&quot;&gt;#13452&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;GMS V1 Checkpoint Lifecycle:&lt;/strong&gt; Added an experimental, isolated GPU memory service V1 process-restore lifecycle preserving weight backing across suspend and resume, selected with &lt;code&gt;--use-v1&lt;/code&gt;. Added exact-ID weight save and load plus a shared checkpoint lifecycle across weights and KV-cache servers (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;4949877991&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/12011&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12011/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12011&quot;&gt;#12011&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5013818120&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/12392&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12392/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12392&quot;&gt;#12392&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5115722457&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/12989&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12989/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12989&quot;&gt;#12989&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5451676984&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14797&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14797/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14797&quot;&gt;#14797&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;GMS V1 Engine Integration:&lt;/strong&gt; Added an opt-in SGLang plugin routing weight and KV-cache allocation through the shared GMS V1 Torch MemPool client, reused for vLLM sleep mode. Fixed SGLang memory saver so GMS workers no longer exit at startup on SGLang v0.5.18 (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5146303332&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13218&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13218/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13218&quot;&gt;#13218&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5354172229&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14360&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14360/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14360&quot;&gt;#14360&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;LMCache Aggregated Serving Example:&lt;/strong&gt; Added a &lt;code&gt;DynamoGraphDeployment&lt;/code&gt; example and integration guide for running aggregated vLLM serving with LMCache MP as the KV cache backend, sharing tensors with the worker over cross-Pod CUDA IPC (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;4566277849&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/10185&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/10185/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/10185&quot;&gt;#10185&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Inference Gateway (EPP)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Reusable EPP Bootstrap Runner:&lt;/strong&gt; Moved the Rust endpoint picker (EPP) process bootstrap into the &lt;code&gt;dynamo-ext-proc&lt;/code&gt; library as reusable &lt;code&gt;run()&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;run_with_selection_service()&lt;/code&gt; functions. Custom linked selection policies can now supply a prebuilt &lt;code&gt;SelectionService&lt;/code&gt; without duplicating Dynamo&#39;s TLS, health, metrics, discovery, readiness, and server setup (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5075350430&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/12720&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12720/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12720&quot;&gt;#12720&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;EPP Graceful Shutdown Handling:&lt;/strong&gt; Added graceful shutdown coordination to the inference gateway ext-proc server. It marks its gRPC health service &lt;code&gt;NOT_SERVING&lt;/code&gt; on SIGTERM or SIGINT and waits a configurable propagation window before stopping new connections, keeping requests off terminating replicas (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5192054380&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13537&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13537/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13537&quot;&gt;#13537&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Operator &amp;amp; CRDs&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;v1beta1 CRD Storage Migration:&lt;/strong&gt; Promoted DCD, DGD, DGDR, and DGDR-scaling-adapter storage to v1beta1 while still serving v1alpha1, then fixed conversion fidelity for the metadata envelope, empty container fields, and preserved service annotations ahead of spec defaults (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;4927699319&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/11904&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/11904/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/11904&quot;&gt;#11904&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5022308312&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/12432&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12432/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12432&quot;&gt;#12432&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5351216236&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14338&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14338/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14338&quot;&gt;#14338&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5464196188&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14855&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14855/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14855&quot;&gt;#14855&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Durable DGD Workload Provider Selection:&lt;/strong&gt; Made workload-provider selection durable by materializing &lt;code&gt;nvidia.com/workload-provider&lt;/code&gt; before reconciliation and treating it as authoritative, and added provider-native &lt;code&gt;providerOverride&lt;/code&gt; fields at the DGD, component, and multinode levels, covering Grove topology configuration (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5112082856&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/12942&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12942/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12942&quot;&gt;#12942&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5155110629&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13273&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13273/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13273&quot;&gt;#13273&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Explicit Multinode Component Roles:&lt;/strong&gt; Added a typed &lt;code&gt;roles&lt;/code&gt; list to DGD and DCD components so multinode leader and worker roles can be declared explicitly and provider overrides attach to the role they configure. Existing implicit multinode manifests remain valid (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5374820746&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14419&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14419/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14419&quot;&gt;#14419&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Performance Optimization Skill Pack:&lt;/strong&gt; Added repository-native agent skills, roles, guides, and rules so an AI coding agent captures a baseline and workload contract. It deploys and smoke-tests it, benchmarks with AIPerf, and proposes one evidence-backed change at a time (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5196595629&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13557&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13557/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13557&quot;&gt;#13557&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5210608593&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13625&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13625/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13625&quot;&gt;#13625&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;DGDR &amp;amp; Profiling Jobs&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;DGDR Profiling Job Overrides:&lt;/strong&gt; Extended &lt;code&gt;applyProfilingJobOverrides&lt;/code&gt; to merge profiling job container overrides by name, so the &lt;code&gt;output-copier&lt;/code&gt; sidecar image can be configured without new CRD fields. Fixed a conversion binding bug and added a &lt;code&gt;kubectl&lt;/code&gt; check to prevent stuck profiling jobs (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;4836851707&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/11392&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/11392/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/11392&quot;&gt;#11392&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5137535625&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13153&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13153/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13153&quot;&gt;#13153&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5406471928&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14589&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14589/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14589&quot;&gt;#14589&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;DGDR KV Routing Support:&lt;/strong&gt; Exposed &lt;code&gt;features.kvRouter.enabled&lt;/code&gt; in the v1beta1 DGDR API, which sets &lt;code&gt;DYN_ROUTER_MODE=kv&lt;/code&gt; on the generated frontend container so users can request KV-cache-aware routing without a low-level DGD override, preserved across v1alpha1 conversion (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5128001481&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13079&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13079/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13079&quot;&gt;#13079&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Append Args in DGDR Overrides:&lt;/strong&gt; Added a &lt;code&gt;$patch: args: append&lt;/code&gt; directive to &lt;code&gt;v1beta1&lt;/code&gt; DynamoGraphDeploymentRequest (DGDR) overrides, so container arguments can be added to a profiler-generated blueprint without restating the generated defaults (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5129688694&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13091&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13091/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13091&quot;&gt;#13091&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Elastic Expert Parallelism&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Elastic EP Leader Wiring:&lt;/strong&gt; Started a Ray head on single-pod elastic EP components in Dynamo Operator, so &lt;code&gt;--enable-elastic-ep&lt;/code&gt; no longer requires the component to be declared multinode. Added a headless leader Service for follower pods to join (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5112243321&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/12943&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12943/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12943&quot;&gt;#12943&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5142830210&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13178&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13178/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13178&quot;&gt;#13178&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dynamo Snapshot&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Shared CUDA CustomStorage Snapshot Layer:&lt;/strong&gt; Added a CUDA CustomStorage operation wrapper shared by checkpoint and restore, bounded helper cancellation through process-group isolation, and persisted and staged the CUDA launch-job file through the source container&#39;s resolved root filesystem (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5030238053&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/12488&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12488/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12488&quot;&gt;#12488&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5111668198&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/12936&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12936/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12936&quot;&gt;#12936&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5113749997&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/12961&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12961/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12961&quot;&gt;#12961&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5151356891&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13252&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13252/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13252&quot;&gt;#13252&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Namespace Bind-Mount Restore Helper:&lt;/strong&gt; Added a C helper and Go mount package for cross-namespace bind mounting, working around Go&#39;s inability to call &lt;code&gt;setns(CLONE_NEWNS)&lt;/code&gt; from a multithreaded runtime. Replaced static path config with on-demand binary injection into the restore container (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5042962014&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/12542&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12542/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12542&quot;&gt;#12542&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5058685996&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/12626&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12626/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12626&quot;&gt;#12626&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Snapshot Shadow Engine Promotion:&lt;/strong&gt; Added a promotion step to the snapshot restore path so restored shadow engines stay paused until a single winner is elected. The winner resumes and registers with the frontend, preventing several engines from claiming the same GPU (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5095862846&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/12869&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12869/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12869&quot;&gt;#12869&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;GPU Memory Service&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;GMS Snapshot Pod Replacement:&lt;/strong&gt; Added an Operator controller that replaces an owned Snapshot restore-target Pod after its native &lt;code&gt;gms-server&lt;/code&gt; sidecar restarts, using UID checks to avoid deleting the wrong Pod. Excluded restore targets from the Grove InterPod failover cascade (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;4823582969&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/11286&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/11286/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/11286&quot;&gt;#11286&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;GMS V1 Allocation Internals:&lt;/strong&gt; Reworked GMS V1 &lt;code&gt;create_mapping&lt;/code&gt; to carve first-fit regions from large client slabs instead of one allocation per Torch segment, and added allocation backpressure. Renamed V1 sockets by device ordinal for stability and supervised one process per device (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5188552644&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13516&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13516/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13516&quot;&gt;#13516&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5153859931&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13262&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13262/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13262&quot;&gt;#13262&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5137747066&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13156&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13156/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13156&quot;&gt;#13156&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5157123918&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13301&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13301/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13301&quot;&gt;#13301&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;GMS KV Layout Commit:&lt;/strong&gt; Added &lt;code&gt;commit_layout()&lt;/code&gt; to the GPU Memory Service, freezing an allocation&#39;s shape while the writer keeps writing, so a standby engine can adopt the same physical KV cache pages instead of allocating an empty pool. Disabled by default behind &lt;code&gt;DYN_GMS_PERSIST_KV&lt;/code&gt; (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5063791081&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/12648&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12648/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12648&quot;&gt;#12648&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Security &amp;amp; Transport&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Operator TLS Auto-Injection:&lt;/strong&gt; Added 10 TLS certificate path fields to Dynamo Operator&#39;s &lt;code&gt;InfrastructureConfiguration&lt;/code&gt;, so TLS and mTLS can be configured once. They auto-inject as NATS and TCP TLS environment variables into every DGD pod, and Dynamo Operator validates the dependency chain at startup (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5226152962&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13689&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13689/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13689&quot;&gt;#13689&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Health &amp;amp; Rollouts&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Configurable Monitor Labels and Paths:&lt;/strong&gt; Added &lt;code&gt;dynamo.metrics.podMonitors.labels&lt;/code&gt;, a configurable operator metrics ServiceMonitor label, and &lt;code&gt;dynamo.metrics.podMonitors.frontendPath&lt;/code&gt; for the frontend PodMonitor and worker &lt;code&gt;http&lt;/code&gt; endpoint, plus Helm unit tests covering the defaults and overrides (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5305721395&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14083&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14083/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14083&quot;&gt;#14083&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5075249320&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/12716&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12716/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12716&quot;&gt;#12716&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5118086567&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13014&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13014/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13014&quot;&gt;#13014&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Forced Grove Scaling Group:&lt;/strong&gt; Added an opt-in &lt;code&gt;experimental.grove.forceScalingGroup&lt;/code&gt; boolean in v1beta1 that renders a single-node component as a Grove &lt;code&gt;PodCliqueScalingGroup&lt;/code&gt; instead of a standalone &lt;code&gt;PodClique&lt;/code&gt;, so each replica becomes independently gang-scheduled and scales as a group (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;4903532237&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/11772&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/11772/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/11772&quot;&gt;#11772&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5352353540&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14341&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14341/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14341&quot;&gt;#14341&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Multimodal &amp;amp; Diffusion&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Colocated EPD Layout and Benchmarks:&lt;/strong&gt; Added a reproducible multimodal benchmark sweep comparing one-GPU Aggregated and colocated EPD serving for vLLM and SGLang, and corrected the vLLM &lt;code&gt;disagg_multimodal_e_pd.sh&lt;/code&gt; GPU layout so it no longer requires a third GPU (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5183954603&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13466&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13466/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13466&quot;&gt;#13466&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5133632514&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13111&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13111/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13111&quot;&gt;#13111&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Frontend Image Decoding for EPD:&lt;/strong&gt; Added opt-in frontend image decoding for multimodal encode-prefill-decode deployments on SGLang and vLLM. Dynamo Frontend decodes images once and hands RGB pixels plus a content hash to the encode worker over a single NIXL transfer, so pixels never relay through the prefill worker (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;4921632100&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/11880&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/11880/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/11880&quot;&gt;#11880&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;4946699703&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/12004&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12004/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12004&quot;&gt;#12004&lt;/a&gt;). Backend decoding stays the default; frontend-decoded video is not yet supported.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Multimodal Sidecar Input Support:&lt;/strong&gt; Added conversion of Dynamo multimodal inputs into vLLM &lt;code&gt;MediaItem&lt;/code&gt; messages, mapping &lt;code&gt;mm_hashes&lt;/code&gt; to reuse vLLM KV-event keys. Extended the path to forward image, video, and audio URLs as vLLM media modalities to both prefill and decode (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;4991302085&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/12214&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12214/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12214&quot;&gt;#12214&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5236567546&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13717&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13717/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13717&quot;&gt;#13717&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;vLLM Custom Encoder Adapter:&lt;/strong&gt; Added a model-aware Qwen3-VL custom encoder adapter preserving pre-merge grids and DeepStack features, with a Qwen3.5 native external-multimodal example. Replaced &lt;code&gt;finish_reason&lt;/code&gt; as an error channel so custom-encoder failures reach callers as a typed HTTP error (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;4914926869&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/11850&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/11850/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/11850&quot;&gt;#11850&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5218312964&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13658&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13658/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13658&quot;&gt;#13658&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5135609027&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13128&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13128/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13128&quot;&gt;#13128&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;vLLM-Omni Realtime Audio Streaming:&lt;/strong&gt; Added realtime session support so streaming ASR models are served through the OpenAI-compatible &lt;code&gt;/v1/realtime&lt;/code&gt; WebSocket API. Added incremental audio delivery for &lt;code&gt;POST /v1/audio/speech&lt;/code&gt; on vLLM-Omni TTS workers, streaming PCM chunks after one open-ended WAV header (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;4912593458&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/11830&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/11830/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/11830&quot;&gt;#11830&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;4969088111&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/12100&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12100/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12100&quot;&gt;#12100&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dynamic LoRA for Omni:&lt;/strong&gt; Added dynamic LoRA lifecycle support to aggregated vLLM Omni workers, including load, unload, and list endpoints, request-time adapter resolution for image and video generation, and registration of loaded adapters as distinct frontend-visible models (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;4858885904&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/11551&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/11551/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/11551&quot;&gt;#11551&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Frontend Media Decoding&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Frontend Media Decoding Upgrades:&lt;/strong&gt; Added a default-on libjpeg-turbo JPEG decoder (when libturbojpeg is present) and an optimized video-rs FFmpeg path decoding frames in native pixel format. Reworked &lt;code&gt;media_io_kwargs&lt;/code&gt; to carry raw JSON for worker-side decoding and kept unknown request fields as an &lt;code&gt;extra_body&lt;/code&gt; passthrough (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;4790534607&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/11157&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/11157/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/11157&quot;&gt;#11157&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;4832538526&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/11364&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/11364/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/11364&quot;&gt;#11364&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5255780869&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13826&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13826/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13826&quot;&gt;#13826&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5254760830&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13817&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13817/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13817&quot;&gt;#13817&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Multimodal Routing &amp;amp; Sidecar Inputs&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Multimodal KV Routing Coverage:&lt;/strong&gt; Added Kimi K3 support to multimodal KV routing, matching routing-side image expansion to the backend prompt shape while retaining existing Kimi behavior. Disabled exact routing when K3 control tokens cannot resolve, and added Qwen video-aware routing (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5173372942&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13371&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13371/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13371&quot;&gt;#13371&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5330940598&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14239&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14239/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14239&quot;&gt;#14239&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;General&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;FastVideo Typed API Migration:&lt;/strong&gt; Updated the FastVideo diffusers example worker to FastVideo&#39;s typed &lt;code&gt;fastvideo.api&lt;/code&gt; interface, replacing the legacy &lt;code&gt;generate_video()&lt;/code&gt; call with structured config objects and CLI flags. Added max video dimension validation and cancellation cleanup for staged MP4 files (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;4450203687&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/9591&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/9591/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/9591&quot;&gt;#9591&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Per-Request Encode Buffer Reuse:&lt;/strong&gt; Reused a single 8 KiB encode buffer across all frames of a push-egress request and read the request-plane codec setting once per request instead of per frame. This cut the encode step for a single-token frame from 312 ns to 232 ns (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5282354352&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13983&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13983/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13983&quot;&gt;#13983&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Engines&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Heterogeneous XPU CPU Disaggregation:&lt;/strong&gt; Added example launch scripts for disaggregated vLLM serving that run prefill on XPU workers and decode on CPU workers, including a router variant with GPU-direct KV transfer. Users can now reproduce heterogeneous prefill-decode deployments (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;4222387891&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/7977&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/7977/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/7977&quot;&gt;#7977&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Neuron NIXL Connector Registration:&lt;/strong&gt; Registered &lt;code&gt;NeuronNixlConnector&lt;/code&gt; from vllm-neuron in the vLLM KV connector protocol registry, so disaggregated prefill/decode serving on AWS Trainium over NIXL routes through Dynamo without additional code changes (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5248524645&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13771&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13771/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13771&quot;&gt;#13771&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Elastic Expert-Parallelism Scale-Up:&lt;/strong&gt; Added runtime elastic Expert-Parallelism scale-up control to the SGLang worker, exposing &lt;code&gt;/engine/control/scale_elastic_ep&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;/engine/control/is_scaling_elastic_ep&lt;/code&gt; routes that integrate a joining group&#39;s GPUs while the primary keeps serving, requiring SGLang v0.5.16 or newer (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5052026368&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/12575&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12575/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12575&quot;&gt;#12575&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Conversation Affinity Rank Owner:&lt;/strong&gt; Added the &lt;code&gt;--conversation-affinity-dp-rank-source {engine,dynamo}&lt;/code&gt; flag and matching environment variable for the TensorRT-LLM backend, so Dynamo can own the initial attention data-parallel placement of a conversation while TensorRT-LLM preserves the resulting affinity (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;4992638285&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/12225&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12225/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12225&quot;&gt;#12225&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;vLLM&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;FPM Self-Benchmark Fidelity:&lt;/strong&gt; Seeded decode self-benchmark points from KV produced by real prefill chains and salted every prompt with a unique &lt;code&gt;cache_salt&lt;/code&gt;, closing the gap between benchmarked and production decode latency on MoE models and providing the scheduler interface the AISimulate v0.12.0 collector requires (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5295504522&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14029&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14029/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14029&quot;&gt;#14029&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;vLLM Self-Benchmark Capacity Sync:&lt;/strong&gt; Synchronized self-benchmark capacity envelopes across attention-DP ranks so all ranks generate identical grids instead of deadlocking. Added variable-length prefill batch sampling behind an off-by-default flag and rejected &lt;code&gt;--benchmark-mode&lt;/code&gt; with data-parallel size above one for dense models (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;4951328718&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/12021&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12021/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12021&quot;&gt;#12021&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5059042217&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/12627&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12627/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12627&quot;&gt;#12627&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5341919125&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14292&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14292/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14292&quot;&gt;#14292&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;vLLM Embedding Worker Pool:&lt;/strong&gt; Added a multi-process Dynamo endpoint pool sharing one &lt;code&gt;EngineCore&lt;/code&gt; per GPU and aligned embedding tokenization with vLLM pooling defaults. Fixed the pool dying at startup with multiple embedding-worker processes and preserved prompt embedding failures as typed errors (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;4973703825&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/12157&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12157/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12157&quot;&gt;#12157&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5382949567&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14449&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14449/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14449&quot;&gt;#14449&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5174382082&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13381&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13381/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13381&quot;&gt;#13381&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Elastic EP Capacity Reporting:&lt;/strong&gt; Added a read-only &lt;code&gt;control/ep_capacity&lt;/code&gt; endpoint reporting how a vLLM worker is parallelized and how many GPUs are idle. Derived the elastic EP scale floor from tensor parallel size instead of a hardcoded minimum of two data-parallel ranks (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5142841032&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13179&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13179/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13179&quot;&gt;#13179&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5111758749&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/12937&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12937/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12937&quot;&gt;#12937&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;TensorRT-LLM&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Response Streaming Path Performance:&lt;/strong&gt; Inverted the TensorRT-LLM decode worker egress path so the Python handler pushes responses into a Rust &lt;code&gt;ResponseSender&lt;/code&gt; backed by a bounded tokio channel, keeping tokio threads off Python. Stripped &lt;code&gt;num_postprocess_workers&lt;/code&gt; from merged engine args before initialization (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5093391081&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/12845&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12845/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12845&quot;&gt;#12845&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5054548011&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/12592&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12592/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12592&quot;&gt;#12592&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;TensorRT-LLM Engine Metrics Accuracy:&lt;/strong&gt; Reported the exact per-request &lt;code&gt;cached_tokens&lt;/code&gt; value from the engine result instead of reconstructing it from block-level metrics, always emitted &lt;code&gt;prompt_tokens_details&lt;/code&gt;, and gated &lt;code&gt;SamplingParams.return_perf_metrics&lt;/code&gt; on &lt;code&gt;--publish-kv-events&lt;/code&gt; instead of hardcoding it (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5197305874&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13567&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13567/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13567&quot;&gt;#13567&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5271937504&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13922&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13922/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13922&quot;&gt;#13922&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;TensorRT-LLM Prefill Completion Publishing:&lt;/strong&gt; Added worker-side first-token completion publication in TensorRT-LLM using the shared endpoint-scoped source, binding the source per request and notifying once on the first substantive token output. When the source is unavailable, the existing Router response fallback is preserved (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5220394109&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13672&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13672/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13672&quot;&gt;#13672&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experimental&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Dynamo Sidecar, the Triton backend, and the SGLang RL rollout contract are experimental in v1.5.0. Their interfaces, defaults, and image layout may change without a deprecation cycle. Dynamo Sidecar runs beside a stock inference engine over its native gRPC API and does not yet match every feature of the in-process backends.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SGLang Sidecar KV-Routing Examples:&lt;/strong&gt; Added experimental aggregated and disaggregated SGLang sidecar deployment examples with exact KV-aware routing, pinning SGLang v0.5.18 as the first version whose gRPC &lt;code&gt;GetServerInfo&lt;/code&gt; reports the structured KV-event descriptor the sidecar requires (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5315812448&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14127&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14127/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14127&quot;&gt;#14127&lt;/a&gt;). Inference through this path returns 500 on the bundled SGLang (see Known Issues).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;vLLM Python Sidecar Launchers:&lt;/strong&gt; Added a wheel-installed &lt;code&gt;dynamo.vllm.sidecar&lt;/code&gt; Python launcher forwarding CLI arguments through the PyO3 backend, plus launch examples and removal of unused OTEL labels. Fixed vLLM-Omni plugin auto-loading that broke every sidecar inference request (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5272051895&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13923&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13923/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13923&quot;&gt;#13923&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5239702862&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13735&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13735/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13735&quot;&gt;#13735&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5261251838&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13864&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13864/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13864&quot;&gt;#13864&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5427161619&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14731&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14731/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14731&quot;&gt;#14731&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Engine-Native SGLang Generate Endpoint:&lt;/strong&gt; Added an opt-in SGLang-native &lt;code&gt;POST&lt;/code&gt;/&lt;code&gt;PUT /generate&lt;/code&gt; endpoint for streaming token-in/token-out inference, replaced the &lt;code&gt;call_tokenizer_manager&lt;/code&gt; passthrough with allowlisted &lt;code&gt;/engine/*&lt;/code&gt; routes, and advertised native generate capability when &lt;code&gt;GetServerInfo&lt;/code&gt; reports the co-located HTTP port (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;4879208219&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/11640&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/11640/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/11640&quot;&gt;#11640&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;4995139920&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/12246&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12246/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12246&quot;&gt;#12246&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5218394238&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13659&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13659/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13659&quot;&gt;#13659&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;TensorRT-LLM Python Sidecar Launcher:&lt;/strong&gt; Added a wheel-installed &lt;code&gt;dynamo.trtllm.sidecar&lt;/code&gt; Python launcher forwarding CLI arguments through the PyO3 backend. Installed the &lt;code&gt;smg-grpc-proto&lt;/code&gt; package before starting the gRPC engine in both the launch script and container, since gRPC is the sidecar&#39;s only transport (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5272084487&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13924&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13924/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13924&quot;&gt;#13924&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5341159318&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14286&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14286/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14286&quot;&gt;#14286&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dynamo Triton Runtime Backend:&lt;/strong&gt; Added a &lt;code&gt;dynamo.triton&lt;/code&gt; backend that serves NVIDIA Triton models through Dynamo, launched with &lt;code&gt;python -m dynamo.triton&lt;/code&gt;, with model discovery, configurable server settings, health checks, logging, metrics, and an example identity model (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5249159162&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13774&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13774/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13774&quot;&gt;#13774&lt;/a&gt;). The backend is experimental and ships as source with its own container recipe. Render it with &lt;code&gt;container/render.py --framework=triton --target=runtime&lt;/code&gt; and build on an &lt;code&gt;nvcr.io/nvidia/tritonserver&lt;/code&gt; release image, selected with &lt;code&gt;RUNTIME_IMAGE_TAG&lt;/code&gt;. No prebuilt Triton runtime image is published for v1.5.0.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SGLang RL Rollout Contract:&lt;/strong&gt; Added an experimental, opt-in reinforcement learning (RL) rollout contract for SGLang workers: &lt;code&gt;nvext.detailed_finish_reason&lt;/code&gt; reports Dynamo&#39;s canonical finish reason such as &lt;code&gt;cancelled&lt;/code&gt; on a pause abort, &lt;code&gt;nvext.extra_fields&lt;/code&gt; carries &lt;code&gt;prompt_token_ids&lt;/code&gt; and sampled logprobs, a &lt;code&gt;--publish-sglang-generate&lt;/code&gt; flag advertises the native &lt;code&gt;/generate&lt;/code&gt; endpoint, the engine&#39;s native pause and memory controls are exposed under &lt;code&gt;/engine/*&lt;/code&gt; and drive Dynamo discovery, and worker &lt;code&gt;output_ids&lt;/code&gt; keep matched stop tokens so training sees exactly what the engine sampled. A Slime example runs two SGLang engines with the in-container sidecar through this contract. Everything in this set is experimental in v1.5.0 and tested only on the example paths (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5215232680&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13640&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13640/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13640&quot;&gt;#13640&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5395157775&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14525&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14525/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14525&quot;&gt;#14525&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5273703377&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13951&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13951/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13951&quot;&gt;#13951&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5345872681&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14317&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14317/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14317&quot;&gt;#14317&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5048825538&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/12562&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12562/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12562&quot;&gt;#12562&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5094263529&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/12856&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12856/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12856&quot;&gt;#12856&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Split gRPC Control Discovery:&lt;/strong&gt; Moved the vLLM sidecar and mocker to vLLM&#39;s split native &lt;code&gt;Inference&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;Control&lt;/code&gt; gRPC services, discovering model identity, capacity, parallelism, KV-event sources, and readiness through &lt;code&gt;Control&lt;/code&gt;. Removed the required model-path configuration while preserving existing launch, deployment, and documentation surfaces (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5076433785&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/12734&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12734/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12734&quot;&gt;#12734&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Deterministic vLLM DP Routing:&lt;/strong&gt; Added forwarding of Dynamo&#39;s selected data-parallel rank as per-request &lt;code&gt;x-data-parallel-rank&lt;/code&gt; gRPC metadata in the vLLM sidecar. Required a unique ZMQ KV-event source per rank when KV routing is enabled, and preserved cache-salt propagation for consistent block hashes (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5076434129&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/12735&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12735/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12735&quot;&gt;#12735&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SGLang Sidecar KV Routing:&lt;/strong&gt; Added event-driven KV routing for the native SGLang sidecar by consuming the KV-event publisher descriptor from &lt;code&gt;GetServerInfo.json_info&lt;/code&gt;. Validated publisher type and topology before worker registration, and preserved native Clap exit behavior for the wheel-installed sidecar launcher (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5198128941&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13579&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13579/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13579&quot;&gt;#13579&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5272274943&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13929&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13929/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13929&quot;&gt;#13929&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Reinforcement Learning&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;vLLM RL Control Plane:&lt;/strong&gt; Routed Dynamo vLLM sidecar reinforcement-learning controls and model updates through vLLM&#39;s native &lt;code&gt;vllm.Control&lt;/code&gt; gRPC API, and added capability-gated pause and resume, sleep and wake, and weight-transfer routes. Published RL worker metadata with world size computed from parallelism dimensions (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5125832327&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13066&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13066/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13066&quot;&gt;#13066&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5153830348&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13261&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13261/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13261&quot;&gt;#13261&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5207083097&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13607&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13607/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13607&quot;&gt;#13607&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5457832511&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14840&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14840/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14840&quot;&gt;#14840&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;RL Route Discovery Endpoint:&lt;/strong&gt; Added an opt-in RL request-plane endpoint behind &lt;code&gt;--enable-rl&lt;/code&gt; or &lt;code&gt;DYN_ENABLE_RL&lt;/code&gt;. It reports a worker&#39;s engine-route names and system-server URL for the SGLang, TensorRT-LLM, and vLLM sidecars plus the Rust mocker, and ships as a versioned discovery response (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5153801887&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13260&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13260/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13260&quot;&gt;#13260&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5207081491&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13606&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13606/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13606&quot;&gt;#13606&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Fault Tolerance &amp;amp; Observability&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Request-Trace S3 Sink Durability:&lt;/strong&gt; Added a native S3 &lt;code&gt;RequestTraceSink&lt;/code&gt; that batches request-trace records as gzipped JSONL behind an opt-in cargo feature. Hardened shutdown to await the final flush and drain outstanding records, and corrected a shutdown drop summary that previously undercounted (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;4906431424&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/11806&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/11806/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/11806&quot;&gt;#11806&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5156977439&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13298&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13298/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13298&quot;&gt;#13298&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5416631250&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14642&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14642/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14642&quot;&gt;#14642&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Model and Worker Readiness Signals:&lt;/strong&gt; Added the frontend-authoritative &lt;code&gt;dynamo_frontend_model_ready{model}&lt;/code&gt; Prometheus metric reporting whether Dynamo Frontend can route requests through a complete serving topology. Fixed Rust backends that left the health route reporting &lt;code&gt;NotReady&lt;/code&gt; after the worker began serving traffic (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5281341558&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13976&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13976/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13976&quot;&gt;#13976&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5383512209&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14458&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14458/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14458&quot;&gt;#14458&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Request Migration &amp;amp; Tracing&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Request Migration Reliability Hardening:&lt;/strong&gt; Added a &lt;code&gt;WorkerOverloaded&lt;/code&gt; error class and classified TCP connection failures so migration retries another worker. Hardened retry bookkeeping against overflow, exposed migration recovery latency via a histogram, and added a span recording migration reasons per worker attempt (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;4880420712&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/11647&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/11647/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/11647&quot;&gt;#11647&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5108140318&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/12927&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12927/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12927&quot;&gt;#12927&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5206434944&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13600&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13600/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13600&quot;&gt;#13600&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5109191079&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/12930&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12930/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12930&quot;&gt;#12930&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;4788635954&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/11133&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/11133/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/11133&quot;&gt;#11133&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;OTLP Export Configuration Hardening:&lt;/strong&gt; Decoupled the stderr console log format from OpenTelemetry export by adding &lt;code&gt;DYN_LOGGING_CONSOLE_FORMAT&lt;/code&gt;, keeping the legacy &lt;code&gt;DYN_LOGGING_JSONL&lt;/code&gt; setting as a fallback. Fixed a panic when &lt;code&gt;logging::init()&lt;/code&gt; ran from a synchronous entrypoint with OTEL export enabled (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5020633001&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/12424&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12424/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12424&quot;&gt;#12424&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;4789441876&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/11143&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/11143/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/11143&quot;&gt;#11143&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Metrics &amp;amp; Readiness&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ThunderAgent Router Observability:&lt;/strong&gt; Added ThunderAgent Router observability through INFO and DEBUG logs for program lifecycle and route decisions, plus new status and metrics runtime endpoints. Added opt-in route proof so operators can confirm traffic passed through ThunderAgent and inspect live program and worker state (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;4988015457&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/12196&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12196/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12196&quot;&gt;#12196&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Model Alias Metric Labeling:&lt;/strong&gt; Resolved aliased model names to the primary served model name in frontend metrics, so &lt;code&gt;dynamo_frontend_model_ready&lt;/code&gt; emits a single readiness series per deployment. Logged each alias claim as it registers to show which worker roles claimed which name (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5354331907&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14364&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14364/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14364&quot;&gt;#14364&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5354441410&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14365&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14365/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14365&quot;&gt;#14365&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Generate Route Frontend Metrics:&lt;/strong&gt; Added frontend metrics for the token-native &lt;code&gt;/inference/v1/generate&lt;/code&gt; route, observing raw engine deltas and split-router metadata, and starting request, queue, and latency lifecycles before frontend processing. Canonicalized model aliases before engine selection so metric labels stay bounded and consistent (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;4834642695&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/11385&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/11385/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/11385&quot;&gt;#11385&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;EPP Cached Token Metrics:&lt;/strong&gt; Added parsing of OpenAI-style usage fields including &lt;code&gt;usage.prompt_tokens_details.cached_tokens&lt;/code&gt; in the inference gateway endpoint picker, exported as &lt;code&gt;dynamo_epp_cached_tokens&lt;/code&gt; Prometheus metrics, and validated that Envoy sets &lt;code&gt;response_body_mode&lt;/code&gt; to &lt;code&gt;FULL_DUPLEX_STREAMED&lt;/code&gt; (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;4915809730&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/11868&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/11868/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/11868&quot;&gt;#11868&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Embedding Cache Metrics:&lt;/strong&gt; Added Prometheus metrics to the vLLM multimodal embedding cache connector, emitting the &lt;code&gt;dynamo_component_embedding_cache_{hits,misses,evictions}_total&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;_utilization&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;_current_bytes&lt;/code&gt;, and &lt;code&gt;_entries&lt;/code&gt; series. Cache hit rate, occupancy, and eviction pressure are now visible in production dashboards under one metric family whichever cache implementation serves the model (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;4942425810&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/11969&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/11969/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/11969&quot;&gt;#11969&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Estimated Reasoning Token Reporting:&lt;/strong&gt; Added an estimate of reasoning-token usage in the shared Chat Completions stream, populating &lt;code&gt;completion_tokens_details.reasoning_tokens&lt;/code&gt; for &lt;code&gt;/v1/chat/completions&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;/v1/responses&lt;/code&gt; in both streaming and non-streaming modes, with positive backend-provided counts still treated as authoritative (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;4981965138&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/12181&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12181/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12181&quot;&gt;#12181&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Engine Request ID Mapping:&lt;/strong&gt; Added an INFO log line in the TensorRT-LLM handler that records the Dynamo request UUID alongside the TensorRT-LLM executor client ID and the disaggregated request ID immediately after submit. Engine-internal timing records can now be joined offline to Dynamo request traces (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5280673561&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13970&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13970/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13970&quot;&gt;#13970&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Performance Modeling &amp;amp; Replay&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Unified AISimulate CLI Integration:&lt;/strong&gt; Registered the Dynamo runner factory and Router and Planner configuration adapters for &lt;code&gt;aisimulate predict&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;aisimulate recommend&lt;/code&gt;, removed the legacy &lt;code&gt;python -m dynamo.replay&lt;/code&gt; CLI, and consolidated dependencies into the published &lt;code&gt;aisimulate&lt;/code&gt; wheel (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5219117131&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13665&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13665/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13665&quot;&gt;#13665&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Mooncake Request Trace Converter:&lt;/strong&gt; Restored the &lt;code&gt;request_trace_to_mooncake&lt;/code&gt; binary in &lt;code&gt;dynamo-bench&lt;/code&gt; behind an opt-in feature, so callers can export Dynamo request traces to reusable Mooncake JSONL files, published through a same-directory temporary file renamed after successful conversion (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5033138941&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/12504&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12504/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12504&quot;&gt;#12504&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Mocker&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Offline Replay Hot-Path Optimization:&lt;/strong&gt; Reduced offline-replay coordinator, cache-index, and completion-event overhead through O(1) worker tracking, an ordered evictable-leaf index, and removed decode accept-length rescans, with public APIs, configuration, and KV-event formats left unchanged (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5005177399&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/12341&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12341/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12341&quot;&gt;#12341&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5084654648&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/12772&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12772/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12772&quot;&gt;#12772&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Mocker KV Accounting Rework:&lt;/strong&gt; Moved per-request KV ownership into move-only backend leases, and switched vLLM and SGLang decode timing to summed logical KV tokens instead of distinct resident blocks. Published buffered KV events at pass completion instead of pass start (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5003939091&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/12329&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12329/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12329&quot;&gt;#12329&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5053174860&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/12583&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12583/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12583&quot;&gt;#12583&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5063846516&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/12653&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12653/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12653&quot;&gt;#12653&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Typed LiveEngine Handoff Control:&lt;/strong&gt; Added a typed &lt;code&gt;LiveEngine&lt;/code&gt; boundary for the Mocker scheduler with configured KV-event and FPM publishers, request registration, and idempotent graceful shutdown. Aligned live disaggregated prefill with offline replay by using the first replay-plan token (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5012739258&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/12380&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12380/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12380&quot;&gt;#12380&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5212598388&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13635&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13635/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13635&quot;&gt;#13635&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Mocker Cached-Token Usage Reporting:&lt;/strong&gt; Added cached prefix token counts, taken when the request is accepted, to vLLM-mode mocker output as &lt;code&gt;completion_usage.prompt_tokens_details.cached_tokens&lt;/code&gt;. Multi-worker simulations can compare the Router&#39;s radix overlap estimate against tokens the scheduler actually reused (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5074401342&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/12711&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12711/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12711&quot;&gt;#12711&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Infrastructure Modernization&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;TLS and mTLS Transport Encryption:&lt;/strong&gt; Added opt-in TLS encryption to the TCP response and request dispatch planes, and covered the NATS transport with matching environment variables and &lt;code&gt;tls://&lt;/code&gt; URL support. Layered opt-in mutual TLS with client certificate verification on top (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;4734462081&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/10921&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/10921/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/10921&quot;&gt;#10921&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5037852043&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/12533&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12533/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12533&quot;&gt;#12533&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5130308491&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13096&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13096/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13096&quot;&gt;#13096&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5191137926&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13528&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13528/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13528&quot;&gt;#13528&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Recipes&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qwen3.8-2.4T-A95B Recipe Support:&lt;/strong&gt; Added the Qwen3.8-2.4T-A95B recipe to the catalog with SGLang and vLLM deployment options for GB200 and GB300, covering chat, agentic, and aggregated configurations (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5132822184&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13105&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13105/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13105&quot;&gt;#13105&lt;/a&gt;). Corrected the model ID to &lt;code&gt;Qwen/Qwen3.8-2.4T-A95B-FP8&lt;/code&gt; across recipe manifests, model download commands, and docs to match the validated checkpoint (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5154009673&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13265&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13265/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13265&quot;&gt;#13265&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Kustomize Recipe Variant Rendering:&lt;/strong&gt; Added a Kustomize workflow for provider and fabric recipe variants that keeps fully materialized &lt;code&gt;deploy-*.yaml&lt;/code&gt; manifests checked in and reviewable. Converted the Qwen3-32B vLLM cloud-provider variants and the Qwen3-235B-A22B-FP8 TensorRT-LLM Blackwell disaggregated variants (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;4752721282&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/10989&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/10989/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/10989&quot;&gt;#10989&lt;/a&gt;). Value-aware Component templates are selected by &lt;code&gt;source&lt;/code&gt; and an overlay-relative &lt;code&gt;path&lt;/code&gt;. They render through strict sandboxed Jinja against a resource index from the built base and materialize as normal local Components, so users need neither Python nor Jinja. Replaced the fixed &lt;code&gt;aws-efa-p8d8&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;aws-efa-p8d16&lt;/code&gt;, and &lt;code&gt;aws-efa-p16d16&lt;/code&gt; Components with AWS instance-type selections, where P5 adds its instance-affinity patch and P6 uses the family defaults (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5135272439&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13125&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13125/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13125&quot;&gt;#13125&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qwen3.5-122B FP8 H200 Recipes:&lt;/strong&gt; Added H200 deployment recipes for Qwen/Qwen3.5-122B-A10B-FP8 on vLLM. Coverage spans an aggregated topology (TP2 with MTP, KV-aware routing, two replicas) and a disaggregated 1P2D topology using NIXL KV transfer over InfiniBand, plus model cache and benchmarking manifests (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;4963316694&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/12088&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12088/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12088&quot;&gt;#12088&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nemotron-3.5-Lightning Deployment Recipes:&lt;/strong&gt; Added &lt;code&gt;recipes/nemotron-3.5-lightning&lt;/code&gt; with vLLM aggregated and disaggregated profiles, TensorRT-LLM aggregated profiles, and model-cache manifests. Added performance traces for B200, GB200, H100, and H200 GPUs, plus documentation and catalog entries so the recipe appears in the recipes overview (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5120837948&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13021&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13021/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13021&quot;&gt;#13021&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nemotron-3-Ultra Refresh Recipes:&lt;/strong&gt; Added 12 Nemotron-3-Ultra Refresh deployment profiles for B200, GB200, and H200 at 256K and 1M context lengths, covering aggregated two-worker and disaggregated topologies, and replaced the legacy Day-0 profiles. The profiles pin the public Dynamo v1.4.0 vLLM runtime image and use KV-aware routing, prefix caching, FP8 KV cache, and hybrid KV cache management (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5146636413&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13226&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13226/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13226&quot;&gt;#13226&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;GLM-5.3-Flash vLLM Recipes:&lt;/strong&gt; Added aggregated and disaggregated 1P1D vLLM deployment recipes for GLM-5.3-Flash, a GLA/KDA hybrid attention model, on GB200 NVL72, covering text and image requests, and added the missing Qwen3.8-2.4T-A95B catalog card (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5264937906&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13899&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13899/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13899&quot;&gt;#13899&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nemotron-3-Super Dev Image Revert:&lt;/strong&gt; Reverted the Nemotron-3-Super vLLM recipes from the generic &lt;code&gt;vllm-runtime:1.3.0&lt;/code&gt; release image back to the dedicated &lt;code&gt;vllm-runtime:1.3.0-nemotron-super-dev.1&lt;/code&gt; build, which carries the model-specific vLLM 0.21.0 patches the recipe was qualified against. Marked the recipe as Dev-only in the Model Early Access Builds reference (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5034100407&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/12520&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12520/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12520&quot;&gt;#12520&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;DeepSeek-V4 Checkpoint Download Parameterization:&lt;/strong&gt; Restored the &lt;code&gt;MODEL_NAME&lt;/code&gt; environment variable in the shared DeepSeek-V4 Pro and Flash model-download Jobs, defaulting to the public FP8 checkpoint that most variants request, and documented the NVFP4 override for the agentic B200 variants. Because each variant mounts the model-cache PVC read-only with offline Hugging Face settings, a checkpoint the Job did not download was not fetchable at runtime and the worker never started (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5123531933&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13034&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13034/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13034&quot;&gt;#13034&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Obsolete Router Flag Removal:&lt;/strong&gt; Removed the &lt;code&gt;--router-reset-states&lt;/code&gt; flag from the DeepSeek V4 Flash and Pro vLLM recipes for B200 and H200, and from the load-only routing documentation, so deployments no longer pass an obsolete option (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5134616328&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13116&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13116/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13116&quot;&gt;#13116&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SGLang GB200 Frontend Args:&lt;/strong&gt; Fixed the Qwen3.8-2.4T-A95B-FP8 GB200 SGLang deployment manifests by removing &lt;code&gt;--model-path&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;--model-name&lt;/code&gt; from the frontend and replacing &lt;code&gt;--dyn-tool-call-parser&lt;/code&gt; with &lt;code&gt;--tool-call-parser&lt;/code&gt;, which previously caused the frontend to exit at startup (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5161710006&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13324&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13324/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13324&quot;&gt;#13324&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nemotron 3.5 Lightning Recipe Refresh:&lt;/strong&gt; Updated the Nemotron 3.5 Lightning recipes to use BF16 weights on B200 and GB200. BF16 measured +80% over NVFP4 with Marlin dense and MoE backends and +12% over NVFP4 with CuTeDSL. Refreshed performance data, corrected the documented context length, added AWS EFA setup instructions, and removed redundant recipes and variants that did not meet the benchmark SLAs (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5173229331&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13370&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13370/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13370&quot;&gt;#13370&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;DeepSeek-V3.2 and Llama-3-70B Recipe Removal:&lt;/strong&gt; Removed the &lt;code&gt;deepseek-v32-fp4&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;llama-3-70b&lt;/code&gt; recipe directories along with their documentation pages, catalog entries, navigation, and dependent feature-benchmark pages for WideEP routing and Llama topology. Refreshed READMEs, codeowners, and remaining references that pointed at the removed paths (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5218868989&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13663&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13663/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13663&quot;&gt;#13663&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bug Fixes&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Frontend &amp;amp; Agents&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;OpenAI API &amp;amp; Validation&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Client Error Status Mapping:&lt;/strong&gt; Returned proper HTTP 400 errors, instead of streamed 200s or plain-text failures, for invalid requests, template failures, out-of-range parameters, and unsupported multimodal content across &lt;code&gt;/v1/chat/completions&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;/v1/responses&lt;/code&gt;, and &lt;code&gt;/v1/messages&lt;/code&gt; (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;4973439786&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/12155&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12155/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12155&quot;&gt;#12155&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;4952608950&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/12036&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12036/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12036&quot;&gt;#12036&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5014352676&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/12404&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12404/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12404&quot;&gt;#12404&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5117333157&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13006&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13006/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13006&quot;&gt;#13006&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5302603121&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14056&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14056/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14056&quot;&gt;#14056&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5132436548&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13102&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13102/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13102&quot;&gt;#13102&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Backend Error Status Propagation:&lt;/strong&gt; Preserved backend 503 and request-rejection status codes instead of masking them as generic 500s, and fixed non-streaming completions so typed errors like &lt;code&gt;Backend(InvalidArgument)&lt;/code&gt; keep their original HTTP 400 status and message (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5015537373&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/12412&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12412/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12412&quot;&gt;#12412&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5114149060&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/12966&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12966/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12966&quot;&gt;#12966&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5073798708&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/12706&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12706/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12706&quot;&gt;#12706&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Single Role Emission in Streams:&lt;/strong&gt; Fixed chat streams emitting &lt;code&gt;delta.role&lt;/code&gt; on every chunk instead of only the first, in both the Rust delta generator and the SGLang streaming postprocessor. Preserved the initial role-only chunk when generation finishes with no content (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5063419306&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/12639&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12639/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12639&quot;&gt;#12639&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5078004519&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/12741&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12741/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12741&quot;&gt;#12741&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Explicit Zero Temperature Preservation:&lt;/strong&gt; Fixed chat-completions request-template handling so an explicitly supplied &lt;code&gt;temperature: 0&lt;/code&gt; is preserved instead of being overwritten by the configured template temperature, keeping deterministic greedy requests from becoming sampled requests (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5063419523&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/12640&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12640/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12640&quot;&gt;#12640&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Per-Choice Tool Dispatch Dedup:&lt;/strong&gt; Fixed streaming tool dispatch dropping &lt;code&gt;tool_call_dispatch&lt;/code&gt; events when &lt;code&gt;n &amp;gt; 1&lt;/code&gt; produced the same tool-call ID across completions, by keying the dedup guard on choice index plus ID. Repeated IDs within one choice still collapse to one event (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5066082047&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/12680&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12680/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12680&quot;&gt;#12680&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Split UTF-8 Character Preservation:&lt;/strong&gt; Fixed multi-token UTF-8 characters showing up as replacement characters (U+FFFD) in the SGLang frontend&#39;s incremental decoding, by tracking committed decode context separately from pending token IDs and committing only at clean boundaries (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5067910701&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/12688&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12688/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12688&quot;&gt;#12688&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Converted Protocol Request Validation:&lt;/strong&gt; Added validation for Responses and Anthropic requests after conversion to the shared Chat format, rejecting empty message lists, out-of-range sampling parameters, and malformed content blocks with 400 before the request reaches the backend (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5087815441&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/12809&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12809/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12809&quot;&gt;#12809&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Runtime Shutdown on Startup Failure:&lt;/strong&gt; Fixed the HTTP and gRPC entrypoints to cancel the distributed runtime before propagating a server startup or bind error, for both discovery-backed and in-process engines. A failed bind no longer leaves the runtime running (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5176203220&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13415&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13415/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13415&quot;&gt;#13415&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cancelled Request Intake Rollback:&lt;/strong&gt; Fixed router state corruption when a request was cancelled while being accepted, which left stale capacity or wait state or overwrote a later request for the same session. Request intake is now serialized per session with guarded rollback (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5196154813&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13553&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13553/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13553&quot;&gt;#13553&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Guided Decoding &amp;amp; Tool Calling&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Reasoning Parser Lifecycle Fixes:&lt;/strong&gt; Fixed reasoning-parser lifecycle bugs that leaked &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;think&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt; text into visible content or dropped it when it should have shown. Covered Nemotron force-nonempty-content requests, &lt;code&gt;include_reasoning=false&lt;/code&gt; responses, interleaved &lt;code&gt;n&amp;gt;1&lt;/code&gt; streams, and text-grammar parsers missing their declared sampling params (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;4821826895&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/11251&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/11251/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/11251&quot;&gt;#11251&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5185793020&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13487&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13487/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13487&quot;&gt;#13487&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;4859812438&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/11563&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/11563/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/11563&quot;&gt;#11563&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5041031303&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/12541&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12541/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12541&quot;&gt;#12541&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Tool Call Guided Decoding Constraints:&lt;/strong&gt; Fixed tool-call guided decoding constraints for vLLM and SGLang across named, forced, and zero-argument tool choices, schemas with reference cycles, double-constrained vLLM reasoning, and Kimi K2 calls wrongly constrained as generic JSON (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5067126121&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/12684&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12684/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12684&quot;&gt;#12684&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5096028775&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/12878&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12878/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12878&quot;&gt;#12878&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5085692884&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/12795&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12795/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12795&quot;&gt;#12795&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5148856900&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13235&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13235/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13235&quot;&gt;#13235&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5250498631&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13785&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13785/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13785&quot;&gt;#13785&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5063419091&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/12638&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12638/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12638&quot;&gt;#12638&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;NvExt Metadata Preservation Fixes:&lt;/strong&gt; Fixed NvExt metadata loss across the frontend, EPP, and legacy streaming tool-call guard, the buffer that holds back partial tool-call markup. The loss dropped &lt;code&gt;cache_salt&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;x-tenant-id&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;nvext&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;engine_data&lt;/code&gt;, token IDs, timing, and routed-expert data from responses. That metadata now survives intact (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5137931211&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13157&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13157/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13157&quot;&gt;#13157&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5239237965&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13730&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13730/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13730&quot;&gt;#13730&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Tool Call Argument Normalization:&lt;/strong&gt; Fixed tool call arguments arriving as JSON strings instead of objects, which produced empty or garbled tool calls in multi-turn conversations for templates like GLM-5.2. Malformed values are now replaced with an empty object and logged (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5004134991&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/12332&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12332/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12332&quot;&gt;#12332&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Truncated Tool Call Recovery:&lt;/strong&gt; Fixed dropped GLM &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;tool_call&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt; XML blocks when &lt;code&gt;max_tokens&lt;/code&gt; truncates a response. The partial block now returns as raw content in both the streaming and non-streaming chat completion paths, so clients no longer receive an incomplete turn (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5004136254&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/12333&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12333/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12333&quot;&gt;#12333&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Unconsumed Control Marker Stripping:&lt;/strong&gt; Fixed unconsumed &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;|...|&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt; control markers leaking into user-visible content when a reasoning or tool parser was active, previously forcing clients to choose between empty &lt;code&gt;reasoning_content&lt;/code&gt; and visible markers. Stripping now applies uniformly to streaming deltas and plain-text responses alike (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5033575213&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/12510&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12510/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12510&quot;&gt;#12510&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;vLLM JSON Tool-Call Fallback:&lt;/strong&gt; Fixed forced vLLM tool choices using the JSON-schema fallback so generated JSON returns as proper &lt;code&gt;tool_calls&lt;/code&gt; instead of assistant content, across required and named choices, streaming, non-streaming, and parallel tool calls (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5102535839&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/12908&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12908/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12908&quot;&gt;#12908&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Request-Scoped Tool Call Parsing:&lt;/strong&gt; Fixed false-positive tool-call parsing by checking each request&#39;s &lt;code&gt;tools&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;tool_choice&lt;/code&gt; fields across Chat Completions, Responses, and Anthropic Messages, disabling ordinary parsers when no tools are declared or &lt;code&gt;tool_choice&lt;/code&gt; is &lt;code&gt;none&lt;/code&gt; (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5168938197&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13359&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13359/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13359&quot;&gt;#13359&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Tool-Call Parser Name Validation:&lt;/strong&gt; Added validation of &lt;code&gt;tool_call_parser&lt;/code&gt; values against Dynamo&#39;s v1 registry and unified parser families during model registration. Returned an error that names the unsupported parser and lists the available ones instead of failing silently during response aggregation (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5257003427&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13828&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13828/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13828&quot;&gt;#13828&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Tokenizers &amp;amp; Model Processing&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Serialized Tokenizer Padding Disabled:&lt;/strong&gt; Fixed models that ship fixed tokenizer padding, like &lt;code&gt;nvidia/NVIDIA-Nemotron-Parse-2.0&lt;/code&gt;, expanding short prompts into padded token IDs and failing context-length validation. Cleared serialized Hugging Face padding when loading &lt;code&gt;tokenizer.json&lt;/code&gt;, matching how Dynamo already clears serialized truncation (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5064030863&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/12656&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12656/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12656&quot;&gt;#12656&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Logprobs &amp;amp; Usage Reporting&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Chat Logprobs Reporting Fixes:&lt;/strong&gt; Fixed OpenAI-compatible chat logprobs so SGLang responses return populated &lt;code&gt;logprobs.content&lt;/code&gt; instead of &lt;code&gt;null&lt;/code&gt;, preserved explicit &lt;code&gt;top_logprobs=0&lt;/code&gt;, and fixed chosen-token and zero &lt;code&gt;top_logprobs&lt;/code&gt; reporting (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5092278340&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/12820&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12820/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12820&quot;&gt;#12820&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5024348248&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/12444&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12444/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12444&quot;&gt;#12444&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5063808928&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/12650&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12650/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12650&quot;&gt;#12650&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5145919036&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13209&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13209/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13209&quot;&gt;#13209&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5414490335&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14621&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14621/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14621&quot;&gt;#14621&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;vLLM Chat-Processor Path Fixes:&lt;/strong&gt; Fixed the vLLM Python chat-processor path, used with &lt;code&gt;--dyn-chat-processor vllm&lt;/code&gt;, so it reports &lt;code&gt;completion_tokens_details.reasoning_tokens&lt;/code&gt; instead of omitting it. Worker-side sampling and grammar rejections now surface their original status and message instead of a generic HTTP 500 (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5273054488&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13947&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13947/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13947&quot;&gt;#13947&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5281821119&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13980&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13980/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13980&quot;&gt;#13980&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Anthropic Messages API&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Anthropic Messages Response Fidelity:&lt;/strong&gt; Brought &lt;code&gt;/v1/messages&lt;/code&gt; streaming to usage parity with &lt;code&gt;/v1/chat/completions&lt;/code&gt;, emitting token usage on every chunk including tokens before a client aborts, reporting &lt;code&gt;cache_creation_input_tokens&lt;/code&gt; as 0 instead of omitting it, with native &lt;code&gt;toolu_&lt;/code&gt; tool-call IDs (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5026230953&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/12473&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12473/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12473&quot;&gt;#12473&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5025803587&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/12472&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12472/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12472&quot;&gt;#12472&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5055339253&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/12614&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12614/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12614&quot;&gt;#12614&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Typed Tool-Call Guard Error Preservation:&lt;/strong&gt; Fixed the v1 streaming tool-call guard collapsing typed backend errors like &lt;code&gt;Backend(InvalidArgument)&lt;/code&gt; to &lt;code&gt;Unknown&lt;/code&gt; by chaining terminal errors instead of reconstructing them. Error messages on &lt;code&gt;/v1/chat/completions&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;/v1/responses&lt;/code&gt;, and &lt;code&gt;/v1/messages&lt;/code&gt; no longer carry an internal prefix (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5272293214&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13930&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13930/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13930&quot;&gt;#13930&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Agents &amp;amp; Request Classification&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SGLang Priority Hint Routing:&lt;/strong&gt; Fixed the SGLang preprocessing path treating all requests as default-priority traffic by projecting &lt;code&gt;nvext.agent_hints&lt;/code&gt; into internal routing hints for priority, strict priority, expected output tokens, and latency sensitivity. Priority-aware Router policies now see SGLang requests correctly (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5059237317&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/12628&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12628/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12628&quot;&gt;#12628&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;LoRA&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;LoRA Adapter Unload Handling:&lt;/strong&gt; Fixed unloading one LoRA adapter making &lt;code&gt;/v1/chat/completions&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;/v1/responses&lt;/code&gt; return 404 for its base model and unrelated models, by deriving endpoint retraction from the live model catalog instead of the removal event alone (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5328566291&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14216&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14216/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14216&quot;&gt;#14216&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5403519044&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14548&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14548/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14548&quot;&gt;#14548&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Shared S3 LoRA Credentials:&lt;/strong&gt; Fixed S3 LoRA credential resolution to use the AWS SDK default provider chain, including shared profiles. Honored &lt;code&gt;AWS_ENDPOINT_URL&lt;/code&gt; through the object-store environment builder, so custom S3 endpoints and profile-based authentication now work for LoRA adapter downloads (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5259444238&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13844&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13844/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13844&quot;&gt;#13844&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Scheduling&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Worker Selection Policies&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Unknown Worker Target Rejection:&lt;/strong&gt; Returned HTTP 400 naming the field and the rejected id when an explicit &lt;code&gt;nvext&lt;/code&gt; worker target is not in the endpoint&#39;s discovery snapshot, across built-in and KV routing, prefill, and route previews (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5464740213&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14858&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14858/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14858&quot;&gt;#14858&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Full Request Body Forwarding:&lt;/strong&gt; Fixed the Endpoint Picker&#39;s KV-router scorer forwarding a reconstructed &lt;code&gt;{role, content}&lt;/code&gt; view instead of the original request body. The reconstruction dropped &lt;code&gt;tool_calls&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;tool_call_id&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;name&lt;/code&gt;, and &lt;code&gt;tools&lt;/code&gt;, and caused multi-turn tool-calling requests to fail with 503 &quot;no healthy upstream&quot; (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;4944086456&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/11991&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/11991/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/11991&quot;&gt;#11991&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Post-Prefill Decode Dispatch Fix:&lt;/strong&gt; Fixed disaggregated serving leaving decode-bound KV blocks pinned until expiry when the client disconnected after remote prefill staged them, instead of dispatching the decode request anyway. Cancellation now keys off staged KV instead of request phase (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5260448349&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13855&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13855/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13855&quot;&gt;#13855&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Router Configuration &amp;amp; State&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Local Output Block Accounting:&lt;/strong&gt; Fixed the KV Router so one frontend replica&#39;s local output-block mutations no longer overwrite shared worker load on the shared load channel with its own state. Prometheus load observation and normal add, prefill, and free lifecycle publishing are unchanged (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5033620872&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/12514&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12514/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12514&quot;&gt;#12514&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Stale Worker Pin Recovery:&lt;/strong&gt; Fixed ThunderAgent session handling so a program pinned to a replaced backend worker is reassigned to a live worker when the request is accepted. Previously it returned HTTP 500 until the session ended or Dynamo Router restarted (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5085205908&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/12783&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12783/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12783&quot;&gt;#12783&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WorkerSet Monitor Lifecycle Scoping:&lt;/strong&gt; Fixed the frontend KV worker monitor task outliving its &lt;code&gt;WorkerSet&lt;/code&gt;. Repeated discovery churn, like LoRA load and unload cycles, had accumulated NATS subscriptions, etcd watches, and per-worker state that grew file descriptors and memory (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5127542105&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13077&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13077/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13077&quot;&gt;#13077&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bounded Worker Load Publishing:&lt;/strong&gt; Fixed Dynamo Router worker-load publishing growing unbounded with request rate by routing snapshots through a single publisher task that keeps only the newest snapshot per worker and data-parallel rank. This bounds pending state by worker count instead. Wire formats are unchanged (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5176873247&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13435&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13435/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13435&quot;&gt;#13435&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Router Weight Download Skip:&lt;/strong&gt; Fixed GlobalRouter model registration to pass &lt;code&gt;ignore_weights=True&lt;/code&gt; in both disaggregated and aggregated modes, so a routing-only process no longer downloads inference weights and delays model discovery (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5271009646&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13916&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13916/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13916&quot;&gt;#13916&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Disaggregated Prefill Error Propagation:&lt;/strong&gt; Fixed invalid-argument errors from the prefill worker flattening into opaque 500 responses in disaggregated deployments, by folding the worker&#39;s error text into the prefill router&#39;s message. Bad sampling parameters or invalid schemas now return 400 (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5303542204&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14063&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14063/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14063&quot;&gt;#14063&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Planner &amp;amp; Profiler&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Actionable Model Path Trust Errors:&lt;/strong&gt; Reported the original filesystem cause with ownership guidance, and the option to set &lt;code&gt;modelCache.pvcModelPath&lt;/code&gt; to the real snapshot path, when a local model path cannot be inspected during DGD materialization, instead of an unhandled error or a silent fallback to a Hugging Face id (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5464945375&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14860&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14860/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14860&quot;&gt;#14860&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;RAPID Profiling Mode Fixes:&lt;/strong&gt; Fixed RAPID profiling for mocker-only DGDRs, which ignored declared &lt;code&gt;spec.workload.isl&lt;/code&gt;/&lt;code&gt;osl&lt;/code&gt; and mis-sized every worker at &lt;code&gt;--max-model-len 6500&lt;/code&gt;. Selected AIC or NPZ profile data via &lt;code&gt;spec.searchStrategy&lt;/code&gt; and passed workload sizes through on the fallback path (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5051964250&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/12573&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12573/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12573&quot;&gt;#12573&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5326818909&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14205&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14205/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14205&quot;&gt;#14205&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Planner KV Hit Rate Namespace:&lt;/strong&gt; Fixed the Planner&#39;s &lt;code&gt;get_avg_kv_hit_rate&lt;/code&gt; querying the wrong namespace on operator-managed deployments, where router metrics carry a suffixed namespace the old filter never matched, sizing as if every request missed the prefix cache. It now falls back correctly (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5184580727&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13480&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13480/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13480&quot;&gt;#13480&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Worker Prefill Completion Events:&lt;/strong&gt; Added &lt;code&gt;MarkPrefillCompleted&lt;/code&gt; publication from LLM workers on first token or first output chunk. Made Dynamo Router consume these marks even with replica sync disabled, so duplicate and stale events become silent no-ops instead of triggering repeated wakes (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5217630239&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13655&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13655/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13655&quot;&gt;#13655&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Planner Plotext Version Pin:&lt;/strong&gt; Pinned plotext below version 6 in the Planner requirements, since plotext 6 no longer exports the top-level &lt;code&gt;plot_size&lt;/code&gt; function used by AISimulate (formerly aiconfigurator), which caused every profiler path to fail in image builds (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5236290750&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13716&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13716/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13716&quot;&gt;#13716&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Profiler DP and Decode Fixes:&lt;/strong&gt; Fixed SGLang prefill workers starving attention ranks by clamping &lt;code&gt;--max-running-requests&lt;/code&gt; to the data-parallel size, and rejected invalid SGLang data-parallel and request-limit values during profiler config generation. Stripped conflicting duplicate vLLM &lt;code&gt;--disaggregation-mode&lt;/code&gt; arguments too (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5353600074&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14351&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14351/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14351&quot;&gt;#14351&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;THOROUGH Profiling Manifest Compatibility:&lt;/strong&gt; Fixed a &lt;code&gt;KeyError: &#39;services&#39;&lt;/code&gt; crash that stopped THOROUGH profiling from deploying its first candidate. &lt;code&gt;DynamoDeploymentClient&lt;/code&gt; now reads component names from either the v1beta1 &lt;code&gt;spec.components&lt;/code&gt; list or v1alpha1 &lt;code&gt;spec.services&lt;/code&gt;, and derives the API version from the manifest (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5406550409&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14591&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14591/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14591&quot;&gt;#14591&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;General&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Router Worker Namespace Suffix:&lt;/strong&gt; Fixed standalone Router worker-endpoint resolution using the wrong namespace by resolving targets through &lt;code&gt;get_worker_namespace()&lt;/code&gt;, including &lt;code&gt;DYN_NAMESPACE_WORKER_SUFFIX&lt;/code&gt; when Dynamo Operator injects it. Dynamo Router still serves its own endpoints from the base &lt;code&gt;DYN_NAMESPACE&lt;/code&gt;, fixing mismatches in Kubernetes deployments (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;4973993153&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/12160&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12160/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12160&quot;&gt;#12160&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;KvRouter Initialization GIL Release:&lt;/strong&gt; Fixed the Python binding for &lt;code&gt;KvRouter.__new__&lt;/code&gt; to release the Global Interpreter Lock (GIL) while waiting for &lt;code&gt;min_initial_workers&lt;/code&gt; to register. Callers can now enforce their own timeouts instead of hanging indefinitely when a worker dies before registering (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5083358673&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/12762&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12762/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12762&quot;&gt;#12762&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Kubernetes Deployment&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Inference Gateway (EPP)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Explicit EPP Replica Sync Port:&lt;/strong&gt; Added &lt;code&gt;DYN_EPP_REPLICA_SYNC_PORT&lt;/code&gt;, defaulting to &lt;code&gt;9092&lt;/code&gt;, so Endpoint Picker replicas bind and dial a fixed peer-to-peer sync port instead of resolving it from Service and EndpointSlice ports. Incomplete EndpointSlices no longer block EPP startup (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5252974407&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13811&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13811/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13811&quot;&gt;#13811&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Operator &amp;amp; CRDs&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;vLLM Multinode DRA GPU Counts:&lt;/strong&gt; Fixed per-node GPU count resolution for components using &lt;code&gt;ResourceClaim&lt;/code&gt;/&lt;code&gt;ResourceClaimTemplate&lt;/code&gt; objects with no scalar GPU resource, which broke multinode vLLM launch flags and TensorRT-LLM &lt;code&gt;mpirun&lt;/code&gt; world size under pure Dynamic Resource Allocation (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;4975053593&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/12166&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12166/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12166&quot;&gt;#12166&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Grove Worker Namespace Suffixing:&lt;/strong&gt; Fixed concurrent Grove worker generations publishing under the same runtime namespace during a rollout, which made discovery reject the new MDC checksum as incompatible. Rendered the worker hash into Grove templates so each generation gets its own namespace (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5084529226&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/12769&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12769/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12769&quot;&gt;#12769&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Immutable Component Type Fields:&lt;/strong&gt; Made the v1alpha1 &lt;code&gt;componentType&lt;/code&gt; and v1beta1 &lt;code&gt;type&lt;/code&gt; fields immutable once set using CRD CEL transition rules, applied to standalone DynamoComponentDeployments and DynamoGraphDeployment components. Updates that alter an existing component type are now rejected, while legacy objects without a type can still initialize it once (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5246743558&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13763&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13763/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13763&quot;&gt;#13763&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Worker Hash Projection Gating:&lt;/strong&gt; Fixed Dynamo Operator completing rolling updates prematurely and writing unreliable annotations, by gating worker hash writes on informer cache confirmation. Required old DynamoComponentDeployments to drain to zero pods before deletion, and scoped DCD discovery accordingly (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5332220840&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14249&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14249/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14249&quot;&gt;#14249&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;KAI Staleness Duration Validation:&lt;/strong&gt; Fixed the platform Helm chart accepting an unset &lt;code&gt;default-staleness-grace-period&lt;/code&gt; unit that passed validation but failed at KAI Scheduler startup. Required the Go duration value &lt;code&gt;-1s&lt;/code&gt; when Grove and KAI Scheduler are installed together (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5424724208&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14722&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14722/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14722&quot;&gt;#14722&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;DGDR &amp;amp; Profiling Jobs&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;DGDR Model Cache Paths:&lt;/strong&gt; Fixed DynamoGraphDeploymentRequest profiling double-prefixing a &lt;code&gt;pvcModelPath&lt;/code&gt; already under &lt;code&gt;pvcMountPath&lt;/code&gt;, producing duplicated paths like &lt;code&gt;/opt/models/opt/models/...&lt;/code&gt; that pointed workloads at nonexistent checkpoints. Relative and legacy leading-slash paths continue to resolve as before (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5031008904&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/12493&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12493/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12493&quot;&gt;#12493&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dynamo Snapshot&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Snapshot Restore Socket Deconfliction:&lt;/strong&gt; Added per-restore remapping of clone-conflicting sockets so one CRIU checkpoint restores repeatedly into sibling engine containers sharing a Pod network namespace, rebinding the CUDA UVM listener and TCP pair. Preserved the &lt;code&gt;restore-complete&lt;/code&gt; sentinel for the kubelet probe (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5096982108&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/12887&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12887/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12887&quot;&gt;#12887&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5073377930&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/12704&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12704/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12704&quot;&gt;#12704&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;vLLM Communicator Checkpoint Hooks:&lt;/strong&gt; Wrapped the vLLM snapshot sleep/wake sequence with &lt;code&gt;checkpoint_prepare()&lt;/code&gt;/&lt;code&gt;checkpoint_restore()&lt;/code&gt; hooks so FlashInfer and NCCL communicators tear down before a CRIU dump and rebuild after restore. Hook failures now propagate so the process dies instead of continuing with half-rebuilt communicators (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;4992679085&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/12226&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12226/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12226&quot;&gt;#12226&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;NCCL Registered Windows Disabled:&lt;/strong&gt; Forced &lt;code&gt;TLLM_NCCL_SYMMETRIC_ZERO_COPY=0&lt;/code&gt; before TensorRT-LLM Snapshot engine initialization and logged a warning when an existing setting was overridden, removing a known checkpoint-unsafe resource from snapshot capture (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5051750917&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/12570&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12570/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12570&quot;&gt;#12570&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Health &amp;amp; Rollouts&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Component-Scoped Topology Spread Validation:&lt;/strong&gt; Relaxed DynamoGraphDeployment webhook validation to accept a deployment topology without &lt;code&gt;packDomain&lt;/code&gt; when at least one component defines its own topology constraint, while still rejecting configurations that set neither (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5024517360&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/12448&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12448/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12448&quot;&gt;#12448&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Multimodal &amp;amp; Diffusion&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;EPD Encode Worker Cache Bounds:&lt;/strong&gt; Fixed the vLLM encode worker&#39;s image embedding cache growing without limit, by routing it through the capacity-bounded LRU &lt;code&gt;MultimodalEmbeddingCacheManager&lt;/code&gt; already used by prefill and decode workers, and removed a hardcoded &lt;code&gt;cache_size=8&lt;/code&gt; limit (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5383036556&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14452&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14452/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14452&quot;&gt;#14452&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5382799573&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14444&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14444/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14444&quot;&gt;#14444&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Multimodal EPD Decode Handoff:&lt;/strong&gt; Fixed the vLLM E/P/D decode handoff dropping mixed image and video media by reloading remaining video and audio when an image placeholder is present. Raised the multimodal NIXL KV lease from vLLM&#39;s 30-second default to 100 seconds (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5394831055&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14522&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14522/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14522&quot;&gt;#14522&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5392800572&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14502&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14502/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14502&quot;&gt;#14502&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;NVDEC Bitstream Filter Support:&lt;/strong&gt; Enabled the H.264 and HEVC MP4-to-Annex-B bitstream filters in the in-tree FFmpeg build while keeping software H.264/HEVC encoders, decoders, and parsers disabled. Restored PyNvVideoCodec NVDEC construction after the media-ffmpeg binding loads the in-tree FFmpeg (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5272509681&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13936&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13936/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13936&quot;&gt;#13936&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Kimi K3 Media Pads:&lt;/strong&gt; Fixed Kimi K3 multimodal handling in the vLLM adapter by expanding each frontend media pad into the checkpoint&#39;s image-placeholder token sequence at the worker. Pad and media mismatches and invalid K3 metadata are now rejected instead of silently misaligning (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5013925170&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/12394&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12394/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12394&quot;&gt;#12394&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Multimodal Embedding Leak Fix:&lt;/strong&gt; Fixed the SGLang worker handler to release received multimodal embedding allocations when image or video item construction fails, so validation errors and cancellations no longer leak receiver allocations (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5199493551&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13587&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13587/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13587&quot;&gt;#13587&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dynamic Diffusion Rendezvous Port:&lt;/strong&gt; Fixed SGLang diffusion workers to pass the allocated NCCL port through the diffusion config as the DiffGenerator master port for image and video workers. It falls back to the SGLang default when no port is provided, which avoids port collisions during concurrent deployments (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5197312424&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13568&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13568/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13568&quot;&gt;#13568&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Multimodal NIXL Buffer Cleanup:&lt;/strong&gt; Fixed &lt;code&gt;MmKwargsNixlSender.cleanup()&lt;/code&gt; hanging forever on cancelled, rejected, or never-read transfers, which kept buffers alive and grew frontend memory until OOMKilled. Cleanup now bounds the wait with a timeout (&lt;code&gt;DYN_MM_NIXL_CLEANUP_TIMEOUT_S&lt;/code&gt;, default 60s) (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5083251793&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/12759&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12759/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12759&quot;&gt;#12759&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Engines&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;vLLM&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;vLLM KV-Router gRPC Flag:&lt;/strong&gt; Fixed the vLLM KV-router sidecar launch scripts to pass &lt;code&gt;--grpc-endpoint&lt;/code&gt; instead of the removed &lt;code&gt;--vllm-endpoint&lt;/code&gt; flag, so aggregated and disaggregated KV-router deployments start with the unified sidecar gRPC endpoint configuration (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5263949498&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13894&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13894/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13894&quot;&gt;#13894&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Codec-Free OpenCV for Image Inputs:&lt;/strong&gt; Rebuilt the vLLM CUDA image&#39;s OpenCV without software video backends so still-image preprocessing keeps &lt;code&gt;cv2.resize&lt;/code&gt; while the image ships no software video codecs, and kept &lt;code&gt;install_media_decoders vllm&lt;/code&gt; as the explicit step that swaps in the full wheel and PyAV (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5354239967&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14361&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14361/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14361&quot;&gt;#14361&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;XPU Wheel and Omni Pin:&lt;/strong&gt; Tagged xpu wheels &lt;code&gt;manylinux_2_39&lt;/code&gt; through &lt;code&gt;auditwheel&lt;/code&gt;, pinned vLLM-Omni to v0.27.0rc1 on the xpu image to match its vLLM v0.27.1, and cleared an inherited metric-port variable in the XPU serve tests so the &lt;code&gt;vllm-xpu&lt;/code&gt; build and tests pass (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5297765811&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14034&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14034/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14034&quot;&gt;#14034&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Decode Handoff Cancellation Preservation:&lt;/strong&gt; Fixed vLLM sidecar cancellation dropping decode requests when client cancellation won the initial race. Kept the decode stream alive until the first token or terminal transfer signal, so the disaggregated NIXL handoff completes (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5076434542&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/12736&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12736/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12736&quot;&gt;#12736&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Decode Worker Engine Shutdown:&lt;/strong&gt; Fixed vLLM decode workers hanging when startup failed after the engine started, by tracking partially constructed resources and shutting down the handler and EngineCore on every worker exit instead of leaving EngineCore alive (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5092662835&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/12829&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12829/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12829&quot;&gt;#12829&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;vLLM Native Generate Capability:&lt;/strong&gt; Added publication of the &lt;code&gt;vllm_inference_v1_generate&lt;/code&gt; runtime capability flag from token-input vLLM prefill, decode, and aggregated workers, so requests to &lt;code&gt;/inference/v1/generate&lt;/code&gt; reach a matching worker instead of failing with a model-not-found error. Text-input, embedding, and incompatible role or type combinations do not advertise the capability (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5096268373&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/12881&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12881/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12881&quot;&gt;#12881&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;vLLM Abort Monitor Cleanup:&lt;/strong&gt; Fixed abort-monitor tasks being retained after normal request completion in vLLM handlers, which caused unbounded memory growth (6.05 GB RSS at 1.9 million requests) and longer GIL waits. Fixed this by tracking, cancelling, and draining child wait tasks (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5214300359&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13637&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13637/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13637&quot;&gt;#13637&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Accelerator-Free Omni Stage Router:&lt;/strong&gt; Fixed the vLLM omni stage router crashing on hosts with no accelerator with &lt;code&gt;RuntimeError: Failed to infer device type&lt;/code&gt;, by detecting the router role before parser construction so it registers only the options it reads (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5354171132&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14359&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14359/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14359&quot;&gt;#14359&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;LoRA Flag Exclusivity Enforcement:&lt;/strong&gt; Fixed vLLM worker argument parsing so &lt;code&gt;--enable-lora&lt;/code&gt; combined with &lt;code&gt;--realtime&lt;/code&gt; or &lt;code&gt;--classify-worker&lt;/code&gt; is rejected instead of accepted, by assigning engine arguments before validation runs. Previously both invalid combinations passed through to worker startup (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5382887560&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14446&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14446/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14446&quot;&gt;#14446&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;vLLM Runtime CRC32C Dependency:&lt;/strong&gt; Added the google-crc32c package to the vLLM runtime container image, which the ModelExpress v0.5.0 vLLM plugin imports at every vLLM startup, and added a build-time guard that verifies the ModelExpress loader registers. This fixes startup failures on XPU base images that lack the package (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5065011025&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/12664&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12664/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12664&quot;&gt;#12664&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;vLLM-RS Binary on PATH:&lt;/strong&gt; Fixed the vLLM sidecar failing to start with a command-not-found error by symlinking the &lt;code&gt;vllm-rs&lt;/code&gt; binary shipped inside the installed &lt;code&gt;vllm&lt;/code&gt; Python package onto &lt;code&gt;PATH&lt;/code&gt;. This keeps it at the same revision as the Python package (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5354296836&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14362&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14362/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14362&quot;&gt;#14362&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SGLang&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Mooncake Backend Preflight:&lt;/strong&gt; Checked that the mooncake &lt;code&gt;ProcessGroup&lt;/code&gt; extension imports and registers before any model I/O, so a worker started with &lt;code&gt;--elastic-ep-backend mooncake&lt;/code&gt; in an image that cannot use it fails at argument parsing with the flag named instead of crashing after model load (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5383576705&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14461&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14461/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14461&quot;&gt;#14461&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pre-Tokenized SGLang Input Handling:&lt;/strong&gt; Added model-aware validation for pre-tokenized &lt;code&gt;nvext.token_data&lt;/code&gt; requests, resolving the max accepted token ID from model or tokenizer vocabulary bounds and returning out-of-range IDs as a client error. Routed pre-tokenized embedding inputs through &lt;code&gt;EmbeddingReqInput&lt;/code&gt; (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5086183552&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/12798&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12798/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12798&quot;&gt;#12798&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5201562196&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13594&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13594/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13594&quot;&gt;#13594&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Conditional Disaggregation Error Code:&lt;/strong&gt; Changed the SGLang backend rejection of the &lt;code&gt;x-bypass-remote-prefill&lt;/code&gt; annotation from a generic 500 internal server error to an HTTP 400 response. Clients now receive the explanatory message directing them to vLLM or TensorRT-LLM for conditional disaggregation (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5052651246&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/12578&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12578/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12578&quot;&gt;#12578&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;DCP-Aware KV Block Size:&lt;/strong&gt; Fixed the router-facing SGLang KV block size using raw &lt;code&gt;page_size&lt;/code&gt; instead of &lt;code&gt;page_size * dcp_size&lt;/code&gt; for decode context parallelism, which made the event converter reject DCP blocks and left KV-aware routing blind (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5084268534&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/12765&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12765/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12765&quot;&gt;#12765&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Temporary Disaggregated Config Cleanup:&lt;/strong&gt; Fixed cleanup of the temporary SGLang YAML file generated for a selected &lt;code&gt;--disagg-config-key&lt;/code&gt; section so it is removed even when configuration merging, topology validation, or argument parsing fails. This prevents &lt;code&gt;dynamo_config_*.yaml&lt;/code&gt; files from accumulating in the system temporary directory after failed worker launches (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5106384055&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/12913&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12913/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12913&quot;&gt;#12913&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Incremental gRPC Stream Contract:&lt;/strong&gt; Switched the SGLang gRPC sidecar to SGLang&#39;s incremental streaming contract, consuming native token IDs and logprob metadata as per-chunk deltas instead of cumulative streams, and enabled &lt;code&gt;--incremental-streaming-output&lt;/code&gt; across launch scripts and manifests (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5240489749&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13739&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13739/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13739&quot;&gt;#13739&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SGLang Min Tokens Mapping:&lt;/strong&gt; Fixed the SGLang backend to map &lt;code&gt;min_tokens&lt;/code&gt; to SGLang&#39;s &lt;code&gt;min_new_tokens&lt;/code&gt; in both the decode handler and the multimodal worker handler. End-of-sequence tokens are now suppressed until the minimum token floor is met, consistent with the TensorRT-LLM, TokenSpeed, and vLLM backends (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5261283511&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13865&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13865/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13865&quot;&gt;#13865&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SGLang Resolved Args Handling:&lt;/strong&gt; Fixed SGLang workers reading raw &lt;code&gt;ServerArgs&lt;/code&gt; after engine initialization, which left values like &lt;code&gt;--page-size&lt;/code&gt; unset and crashed the KV event publisher with a &lt;code&gt;TypeError&lt;/code&gt; on a &lt;code&gt;None&lt;/code&gt; block size. Dynamo now reads the resolved configuration view instead (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5268904472&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13905&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13905/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13905&quot;&gt;#13905&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SGLang Config Parser Compatibility:&lt;/strong&gt; Fixed the SGLang integration importing &lt;code&gt;ConfigArgumentMerger&lt;/code&gt; from a path that broke on current nightlies, by preferring the relocated &lt;code&gt;sglang.srt.utils&lt;/code&gt; module through a compatibility shim. Dynamo now works with both pinned SGLang releases and newer layouts (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5302511206&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14054&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14054/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14054&quot;&gt;#14054&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Per-Rank NIXL Telemetry Ports:&lt;/strong&gt; Fixed SGLang co-located ranks crashing on a shared NIXL exporter port by treating &lt;code&gt;NIXL_TELEMETRY_PROMETHEUS_PORT&lt;/code&gt; as the base of a per-rank range with bounds checks against overflow. Disaggregated SGLang deployments now reach Ready with KV-transfer counters intact (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5340788278&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14284&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14284/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14284&quot;&gt;#14284&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;TensorRT-LLM&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Zero Prompt Logprobs Preservation:&lt;/strong&gt; Fixed the TensorRT-LLM request translation path so an explicit &lt;code&gt;prompt_logprobs=0&lt;/code&gt; is forwarded to the engine instead of being treated as omitted. Callers requesting log probabilities for selected prompt tokens only now receive them (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5068388438&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/12689&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12689/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12689&quot;&gt;#12689&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Prefill Stop Condition Handling:&lt;/strong&gt; Fixed the TensorRT-LLM handler overriding only &lt;code&gt;max_tokens&lt;/code&gt; during prefill instead of applying full stop conditions, so a request with &lt;code&gt;ignore_eos=true&lt;/code&gt; whose first token was EOS terminated immediately with HTTP 200 and no content. Stop conditions now pass through unchanged (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5177814124&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13442&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13442/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13442&quot;&gt;#13442&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cancellation Listener Cleanup Fix:&lt;/strong&gt; Fixed a leak in the TensorRT-LLM backend where per-request client cancellation and service shutdown listeners were not stopped after a request completed normally. The leak accumulated tasks and memory under sustained traffic and ended in worker out-of-memory failures (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5267531111&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13901&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13901/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13901&quot;&gt;#13901&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Context-Length Precedence Fix:&lt;/strong&gt; Fixed the TensorRT-LLM sidecar discarding a configured &lt;code&gt;--context-length&lt;/code&gt; (or &lt;code&gt;TRTLLM_CONTEXT_LENGTH&lt;/code&gt;) whenever &lt;code&gt;GetModelInfo&lt;/code&gt; reported a positive value, so the operator-supplied value now wins with a warning naming both numbers when they disagree (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5382950170&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14450&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14450/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14450&quot;&gt;#14450&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Environment-Independent Triton JIT:&lt;/strong&gt; Fixed a &lt;code&gt;cuda.h: No such file or directory&lt;/code&gt; failure in Triton&#39;s &lt;code&gt;cuda_utils&lt;/code&gt; on SSH-launched multinode TensorRT-LLM worker ranks. Restored Triton&#39;s default lookup layout with symlinks to the CUDA toolkit&#39;s &lt;code&gt;cuda.h&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;ptxas&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;cuobjdump&lt;/code&gt;, and &lt;code&gt;nvdisasm&lt;/code&gt;, so JIT compilation no longer depends on image environment variables (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5465430829&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14865&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14865/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14865&quot;&gt;#14865&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Reinforcement Learning&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Worker Discovery Visibility Fixes:&lt;/strong&gt; Fixed &lt;code&gt;materialization_fingerprint&lt;/code&gt; hashing fields the frontend overrides, which split a &lt;code&gt;WorkerSet&lt;/code&gt; into cohorts and hid the model from &lt;code&gt;/v1/models&lt;/code&gt; during rolling upgrades, and reworked RL worker discovery to resolve a &lt;code&gt;NamespaceFilter&lt;/code&gt; on Kubernetes (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5383006155&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14451&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14451/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14451&quot;&gt;#14451&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5383289415&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14455&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14455/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14455&quot;&gt;#14455&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Fault Tolerance &amp;amp; Observability&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Worker Shutdown Request Migration:&lt;/strong&gt; Fixed requests interrupted by a worker shutdown terminating as clean cancellations instead of migrating, by briefly holding the terminal cancellation frame so the shutdown failure reaches the migration layer. Client-started cancellations and ordinary response streams keep their existing behavior (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5273924149&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13952&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13952/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13952&quot;&gt;#13952&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Worker Sidecar Metrics Scraping:&lt;/strong&gt; Added an &lt;code&gt;http&lt;/code&gt; port endpoint to the &lt;code&gt;dynamo-worker&lt;/code&gt; PodMonitor so &lt;code&gt;dynamo_frontend_*&lt;/code&gt; metrics from the frontend sidecar on Gateway API and EPP worker pods reach Prometheus, restoring the cached-token Grafana panel (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;4943207901&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/11981&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/11981/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/11981&quot;&gt;#11981&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;HTTP Graceful Shutdown Guard:&lt;/strong&gt; Fixed &lt;code&gt;HttpService::run()&lt;/code&gt; to register and hold a graceful-shutdown guard for the lifetime of the service. The runtime no longer cancels discovery watches while in-flight requests and long-running streams are still draining after SIGTERM (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;4951977699&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/12031&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12031/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12031&quot;&gt;#12031&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Raced Final Marker Errors:&lt;/strong&gt; Fixed false-positive worker errors when the trailing &lt;code&gt;complete_final&lt;/code&gt; marker lost a race with frontend teardown on successful streaming requests, which incremented &lt;code&gt;dynamo_component_errors_total{error_type=&quot;publish_final&quot;}&lt;/code&gt;. Those sends now log at DEBUG, while genuine dropped connections detected through &lt;code&gt;kill()&lt;/code&gt; are still counted (#12374).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Prometheus Name Generator Sync:&lt;/strong&gt; Fixed the Prometheus name generator and its Python and Rust sync so metric names dropped by the codegen gap (&lt;code&gt;transport&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;frontend_service&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;work_handler&lt;/code&gt;, and tokenizer cache names) are restored. Made the generator fail on a name collision instead of silently dropping a constant (#12745, #13283).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bounded TCP Accept Backoff:&lt;/strong&gt; Added exponential backoff and rate-limited logging for TCP response server accept failures from file-descriptor or kernel memory exhaustion. This replaced a busy retry loop that spun at microsecond cadence and repeated the same warning every iteration (#13146).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Administrative Route Lifecycle Hardening:&lt;/strong&gt; Gated Backend SDK engine control, engine update, and model-taint routes on the worker serving lifecycle and serialized administrative mutations with discovery transitions, so requests no longer race worker startup, discovery registration, or shutdown (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5153755273&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13259&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13259/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13259&quot;&gt;#13259&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Typed Backend Refusal Errors:&lt;/strong&gt; Fixed unservable requests, like multimodal input sent to a backend without multimodal support, returning a generic HTTP 500 instead of a useful error. Worker refusals now carry a typed error, and SGLang and TensorRT-LLM guards raise &lt;code&gt;InvalidArgument&lt;/code&gt; (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5385459111&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/14467&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14467/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14467&quot;&gt;#14467&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Performance Modeling &amp;amp; Replay&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Public Mocker Worker CLI:&lt;/strong&gt; Restored the &lt;code&gt;python3 -m dynamo.mocker&lt;/code&gt; live worker CLI and migrated in-repo launchers, manifests, and documentation to it, while retaining &lt;code&gt;python3 -m dynamo.mocker._worker&lt;/code&gt; as a compatibility shim for existing 1.5 configurations (#14230).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;General&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Shared-Source Served Aliases:&lt;/strong&gt; Allowed non-LoRA workers with different served names to register on the same endpoint when they advertise the same source path, with each served name selecting its own worker group, while base and LoRA name collisions stay rejected (#14857).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;CUDA and uv Dependency Pinning:&lt;/strong&gt; Pinned &lt;code&gt;cupy&lt;/code&gt; to the &lt;code&gt;cuda13x&lt;/code&gt; distribution in the &lt;code&gt;sglang&lt;/code&gt; extra and enforced the CUDA major version, removing the last CUDA 12 reference, and declared mutually exclusive backend extras through &lt;code&gt;tool.uv.conflicts&lt;/code&gt; (#13650, #12933).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Discovery Instance State Consistency:&lt;/strong&gt; Reworked Kubernetes discovery to emit &lt;code&gt;Added&lt;/code&gt; as an upsert for same-ID endpoint updates, propagating metadata changes instead of detecting only added or removed IDs. Restored first-wins model deployment card acceptance so an incompatible card no longer withdraws the set (#12574, #14632).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Configured Dynamo Runtime Propagation:&lt;/strong&gt; Handed the configured Dynamo runtime to the PyO3 async bridge so &lt;code&gt;DYN_RUNTIME_NUM_WORKER_THREADS&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;DYN_RUNTIME_MAX_BLOCKING_THREADS&lt;/code&gt; apply to the frontend-serving runtime instead of a second Tokio runtime, and pinned mocker startup to the owning executor (#13849, #13352).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bundled Runtime Dependency Refresh:&lt;/strong&gt; Refreshed third-party packages the SGLang and vLLM runtime images inherit from their base images, raising the bundled mooncake transfer engine and flooring &lt;code&gt;cryptography&lt;/code&gt; for vLLM to pick up an updated etcd stack (#14082).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;New Release Artifacts&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Unified Sidecar Image (Experimental):&lt;/strong&gt; Shipped one CPU-only, multi-arch &lt;code&gt;dynamo-sidecar&lt;/code&gt; image carrying the SGLang, TensorRT-LLM, and vLLM sidecar executables, replacing the per-engine images. Select the engine with the container command (&lt;code&gt;dynamo-sglang-sidecar&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;dynamo-trtllm-sidecar&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;dynamo-vllm-sidecar&lt;/code&gt;); the engine stays in its own GPU container (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5250127311&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13781&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13781/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13781&quot;&gt;#13781&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5271507664&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13917&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13917/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13917&quot;&gt;#13917&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Rust EPP Frontend Image:&lt;/strong&gt; Shipped the Rust Endpoint Picker binary inside the Dynamo Frontend image at &lt;code&gt;/epp&lt;/code&gt;, replacing the Go EPP. A standalone &lt;code&gt;dynamo-epp&lt;/code&gt; image is planned for a later release (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;4832049685&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/11355&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/11355/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/11355&quot;&gt;#11355&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nightly Helm Charts:&lt;/strong&gt; Published nightly Dynamo Helm charts through both ChartMuseum and OCI so nightly deployments no longer need a local chart build (#12962).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Standalone Snapshot Operator:&lt;/strong&gt; Moved Dynamo Snapshot to its own &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/snapshot&quot;&gt;repository&lt;/a&gt; and chart, shipped as Snapshot v0.1.0 at &lt;code&gt;oci://ghcr.io/ai-dynamo/snapshot/snapshot:0.1.0&lt;/code&gt;. The &lt;code&gt;PodSnapshot&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;PodSnapshotContent&lt;/code&gt; CRDs and their reconciler now come from that operator. The Dynamo platform chart can pull it in as a subchart with &lt;code&gt;global.snapshot.install=true&lt;/code&gt; for evaluation; production deployments should install it separately (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5142245456&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13177&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13177/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13177&quot;&gt;#13177&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AISimulate v0.12.0:&lt;/strong&gt; Consumed &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/aisimulate&quot;&gt;AISimulate&lt;/a&gt; as a standalone release with one unified CLI, replacing the separate aiconfigurator wheels (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5184510788&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/13478&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13478/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/13478&quot;&gt;#13478&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Documentation&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Release and Version Page Updates:&lt;/strong&gt; Promoted the docs current-release surfaces through v1.4.0, v1.4.1, and v1.4.2, and refreshed the README community events table, Slack badge, and Dynamo Enterprise support section. Corrected nightly release artifact listings and hardened docs CI with a lint gate, verified-commit checks, test ownership, and a preview-build flake fix (#13269, #12752, #13678, #13999, #13310, #13344, #12469, #12498, #13720, #12737, #13843, #13854, #12528, #12763, #13882, #12388).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Generated API Reference Docs:&lt;/strong&gt; Added deterministic, CI-gated API reference generation for Python, Rust crates, and Kubernetes CRDs as native Fern MDX. Moved generation to publish time so source PRs no longer carry machine-generated content, and fixed stale CRD reference links and a reference-checker crash (#12110, #13556, #13035, #12985, #13320, #12815, #12342).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Support Matrix and Deploy Guides:&lt;/strong&gt; Replaced the CUDA driver picker with a generated support matrix reporting containers-versus-wheels-only scope, and defined the N-2 worker/frontend compatibility window. Aligned the Kubernetes build selector with the CLI guide, and added Vanilla vLLM GAIE, MatrixHub, and deploy contributing guides (#12215, #12529, #12479, #13668, #12800, #12894, #13886, #10957, #11197, #11700, #12729).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Router and KV Routing Docs:&lt;/strong&gt; Refreshed Dynamo Router cost, scheduling, event-recovery, topology-aware KV transfer, and standalone-mode documentation to match the current implementation. Added a runnable custom worker-selection policy walkthrough, corrected the Selection API environment variable, and reorganized the Router docs into six task-oriented sections (#12635, #12634, #12431, #12992, #13039, #13915, #13015).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Docs Navigation and Fern Styling:&lt;/strong&gt; Restructured guides around reader intent with dedicated Kubernetes, Local, and backend areas, and fixed Fern home page and navigation styling defects. Repointed the Fern CLI and dead SGLang and Helm chart links, and added tab-aligned authoring templates (#12993, #12373, #12410, #12436, #13942, #13973, #12539, #12615, #12861, #13115, #12817, #12823, #13138, #12668, #12426).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;RL and Agent Skill Docs:&lt;/strong&gt; Added a reinforcement learning integration guide covering rollout inference and the SGLang-compatible &lt;code&gt;/generate&lt;/code&gt; API. Restructured the guides into a docs-only set spanning trainers, KV-aware routing, and simulation, and corrected the shipped agent optimization skill pack (#11381, #13127, #13912, #13608, #13639, #13067).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Operator, CRD, and EPP Docs:&lt;/strong&gt; Clarified &lt;code&gt;scalingAdapter&lt;/code&gt; and worker-hash rollout semantics per API version, and refreshed CRD YAML and image tags to 1.4.0. Documented the webhook failure-policy default, and announced the Go Endpoint Picker deprecation with Rust EPP migration guidance (#12986, #13270, #12744, #12563, #13243, #13244, #13401).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Backend Flag and Config Corrections:&lt;/strong&gt; Removed retired vLLM prefill and decode worker flags in favor of &lt;code&gt;--disaggregation-mode&lt;/code&gt;, and replaced stale benchmark-granularity flags with the six sampling flags the parser exposes. Fixed the SGLang &lt;code&gt;MAX_TOTAL_TOKENS&lt;/code&gt; description, and clarified SGLang LoRA support status (#12568, #12581, #13036, #13271, #14057, #13822).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Recipe and Multimodal Serving Docs:&lt;/strong&gt; Added catalog-owned image provenance metadata for six recipes, published Qwen3.5-122B-A10B and GLM-5.3 recipe pages, and added a multimodal serving guide covering parallel image decoding and custom vision encoders across backends (#13232, #13469, #12931, #13995, #12417, #13651, #13673).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Planner, Profiler, and Observability Docs:&lt;/strong&gt; Synchronized Planner, Profiler, DGDR, and SPICA documentation with the current implementation, and documented profiler component names and the unified AISimulate CLI. Corrected the request-trace S3 sink behavior, and cleaned up 151 rustdoc warnings and the external and research publications pages (#12408, #13446, #14148, #14623, #13223, #12945).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;verl Guide Version Bounds:&lt;/strong&gt; Bounded the verl reinforcement-learning guide to vLLM v0.26.0, added &lt;code&gt;flash-attn&lt;/code&gt; as an explicit prerequisite, and passed the three &lt;code&gt;_per_gpu&lt;/code&gt; micro-batch overrides the pinned verl requires, so readers no longer hit import errors on the v1.5.0 vLLM pin (#14571).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Version Upgrades&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Major Dependencies&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;vLLM:&lt;/strong&gt; Upgraded from v0.26.0 to &lt;strong&gt;v0.28.0&lt;/strong&gt; (#13846).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SGLang:&lt;/strong&gt; Upgraded from v0.5.16 to &lt;strong&gt;v0.5.18&lt;/strong&gt; (#13343, #13643).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;TensorRT-LLM:&lt;/strong&gt; Upgraded from v1.3.0rc22 to &lt;strong&gt;v1.3.0rc25&lt;/strong&gt; (#12532, #13093, #14043).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;vLLM-Omni:&lt;/strong&gt; Upgraded from v0.26.0rc1 to &lt;strong&gt;v0.28.0rc1&lt;/strong&gt; (#14051).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Other Dependencies&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AIPerf:&lt;/strong&gt; Updated from v0.10.0 to &lt;strong&gt;v0.12.0&lt;/strong&gt; (#14492).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AISimulate:&lt;/strong&gt; Updated from aiconfigurator v0.11.0 to &lt;strong&gt;v0.12.0&lt;/strong&gt; (#14867, #15012).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Snapshot:&lt;/strong&gt; Updated from bundled to &lt;strong&gt;v0.1.0&lt;/strong&gt; (#14471).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Grove and KAI Scheduler:&lt;/strong&gt; Updated Grove from v0.1.0-alpha.12-rc1 to &lt;strong&gt;v0.1.0-alpha.13&lt;/strong&gt; and KAI Scheduler from v0.13.4 to &lt;strong&gt;v0.17.0&lt;/strong&gt; (#14553).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ModelExpress:&lt;/strong&gt; Updated from v0.4.x to &lt;strong&gt;v0.5.0&lt;/strong&gt; (#12455).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;dynamo-protocols:&lt;/strong&gt; Updated from v5.0.1 to &lt;strong&gt;v5.4.0&lt;/strong&gt; (#12523, #13768).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;dynamo-renderer:&lt;/strong&gt; Updated from v4.0.0 to &lt;strong&gt;v5.1.0&lt;/strong&gt; (#13662).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;dynamo-tokenizers:&lt;/strong&gt; Updated from v1.5.4 to &lt;strong&gt;v1.8.0&lt;/strong&gt; (#12707).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;dynamo-parsers:&lt;/strong&gt; Updated from v7.0.1 to &lt;strong&gt;v8.1.0&lt;/strong&gt; (#12576).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;transformers:&lt;/strong&gt; Updated from unpinned to &lt;strong&gt;5.14.1 (pinned below 5.15 for the vLLM extra)&lt;/strong&gt; (#13059).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;async-openai:&lt;/strong&gt; Updated from 0.40 to &lt;strong&gt;0.41&lt;/strong&gt; (#12069).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;blake3:&lt;/strong&gt; Updated from 1.8.x to &lt;strong&gt;1.8.7&lt;/strong&gt; (#13597).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;velo:&lt;/strong&gt; Updated from 0.11 to &lt;strong&gt;0.12.0&lt;/strong&gt; (#14266).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;aiohttp:&lt;/strong&gt; Updated from a mixed set across images to &lt;strong&gt;3.14.3&lt;/strong&gt; (#13132).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;pillow:&lt;/strong&gt; Updated from 12.2.0 in the Frontend and Planner images to &lt;strong&gt;12.3.0&lt;/strong&gt; (#13741).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;protobuf and tritonclient:&lt;/strong&gt; Updated from protobuf 5.29.6 and tritonclient 2.71.0 to &lt;strong&gt;protobuf 6.33.6 and tritonclient 2.72.0&lt;/strong&gt; (#14491).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;google.golang.org/grpc (operator):&lt;/strong&gt; Updated from 1.82.1 to &lt;strong&gt;1.83.2&lt;/strong&gt; (#14280, #14549).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;quinn-proto:&lt;/strong&gt; Updated from 0.11.14 to &lt;strong&gt;0.11.17&lt;/strong&gt; (#11350).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;NIXL (Dynamo runtime):&lt;/strong&gt; Updated from v1.0.1 to &lt;strong&gt;v1.3.2&lt;/strong&gt;, aligning the Rust runtime &lt;code&gt;nixl-sys&lt;/code&gt; link with the Frontend and vLLM images (#13772).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Known Issues&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Backend (SGLang)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SGLang Sidecar Inference 500 Errors&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Every inference request sent to the SGLang sidecar fails with HTTP 500 and the error &lt;code&gt;&#39;GenerateReqInput&#39; object has no attribute &#39;batch_size&#39;&lt;/code&gt;. Startup, registration and discovery succeed on the same binaries, so only the generate path is affected; the cause is a protocol mismatch between the sidecar&#39;s request handling and the bundled SGLang version, which is corrected in upstream SGLang v0.5.19. No workaround is available yet.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Missing Prompt Logprobs under Disaggregation&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;With the SGLang backend in disaggregated (prefill/decode) serving, requests to the engine-native &lt;code&gt;/generate&lt;/code&gt; endpoint that set &lt;code&gt;return_logprob&lt;/code&gt; are accepted but come back with no prompt logprobs. No error or warning explains the omission, while the same request in aggregated serving returns them. The prompt logprobs are produced on the prefill worker and are not propagated through the decode path. The request handler does not surface a diagnostic when they are absent, so callers cannot tell an unsupported option from an empty result. The missing logprobs are a known gap in the current engine-native generate path and are not scheduled for a fix in this release. No workaround is available yet.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SGLang DCP Worker Request Crash&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;SGLang workers launched with &lt;code&gt;--dcp-size&lt;/code&gt; crash on every real completion request with &lt;code&gt;RuntimeError: shape &#39;[-1, 1024]&#39; is invalid for input of size 5632&lt;/code&gt;. The attention tensor-parallel size does not account for &lt;code&gt;dcp_size&lt;/code&gt;, so it mismatches the DCP-aware head split of the KV pool. The root cause is in SGLang. &lt;strong&gt;Workaround:&lt;/strong&gt; do not set &lt;code&gt;--dcp-size&lt;/code&gt; on SGLang workers in v1.5.0. The fix is targeted for v1.6.0 with the next SGLang bump.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Backend (vLLM)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;RL Weight Version Tracking Drift&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In reinforcement learning workflows on the vLLM backend, the reported weight version can disagree with the weights actually loaded in the engine, so downstream consumers may treat stale weights as current.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;CLI &amp;amp; Tooling&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Replay Module Entrypoint Removal&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Scripts and test suites that invoke &lt;code&gt;python -m dynamo.replay&lt;/code&gt; now fail because the module no longer provides a CLI entry point. The replay CLI moved into the AISimulate wheel with no compatibility shim. &lt;strong&gt;Workaround:&lt;/strong&gt; migrate to &lt;code&gt;aisimulate predict --stack dynamo --config &amp;lt;file&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt;. It takes a YAML config instead of the previous command-line arguments and does not support online mode. See &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/blob/main/docs/fern/pages/cli/operations/simulation-with-dynosim/dynosim-replay.mdx&quot;&gt;the replay guide&lt;/a&gt; for usage.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Frontend&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bare 500 on Request Errors&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;When a request-level error is returned by the backend, clients receive a bare HTTP 500 with no explanatory message, so the actual failure reason is not visible in the response.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Planner&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Thorough-Mode MoE GPU Overrun&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;When the deployment recommender is run in thorough mode against a Mixture-of-Experts model, for example Qwen/Qwen3-30B-A3B, the enumerated profiling candidates can require more GPUs than the cluster GPU budget, so candidate configurations that cannot be deployed are still produced.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Mocker Thorough Profiling GPU Crash&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;When a DynamoGraphDeploymentRequest sets &lt;code&gt;features.mocker.enabled=true&lt;/code&gt; together with &lt;code&gt;pre_deployment_sweeping_mode=thorough&lt;/code&gt;, the SLA profiler still launches a real GPU worker deployment. That pod enters &lt;code&gt;CrashLoopBackOff&lt;/code&gt; for lack of GPUs after about 40 seconds and the profiling job aborts. The interpolation path is missing the mocker check, so a GPU-free run still creates a GPU deployment. &lt;strong&gt;Workaround:&lt;/strong&gt; use &lt;code&gt;pre_deployment_sweeping_mode=rapid&lt;/code&gt; for GPU-free profiling with the mocker.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Mocker Perf Model Startup Crash&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Launching &lt;code&gt;dynamo.mocker&lt;/code&gt; with &lt;code&gt;--aic-perf-model&lt;/code&gt; crashes on startup instead of serving mock requests. &lt;strong&gt;Workaround:&lt;/strong&gt; launch the mocker without &lt;code&gt;--aic-perf-model&lt;/code&gt;, or run performance modeling through &lt;code&gt;aisimulate predict&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Runtime &amp;amp; Router&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Explicit Prefill Pin Request Failure&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Requests that specify an explicit prefill target fail hard when that target is locally inhibited: the router neither dispatches the request to the pinned worker nor falls back to another prefill worker.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Upstream Limitations&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;FP8 MoE Weight Load Crash&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Serving Qwen3-30B-A3B in its FP8 MoE variant on the vLLM backend crashes during model weight loading, with a shape mismatch raised from the expert weight loader (&lt;code&gt;routed_experts._load_w13&lt;/code&gt;, tensor a(6) vs b(8)). The failure reproduces on H100, B200, and GB200. The crash reproduces on bare vLLM at the pinned version, so the fix is upstream. This FP8 variant is not covered by any Dynamo recipe, test, or model catalog entry. The non-FP8 Qwen3-30B-A3B checkpoint is unaffected. No workaround is available yet.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Disagg Prefill Worker Sleep Failure&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In vLLM disaggregated deployments, putting a prefill worker to sleep fails after it has served inference traffic, so the worker cannot be freed or scaled down.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dynamo Enterprise&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A curated set of v1.5.0 release artifacts is also published under the &lt;code&gt;-enterprise&lt;/code&gt; suffix in the &lt;a href=&quot;https://catalog.ngc.nvidia.com/orgs/nvidia/ai-dynamo/collections/dynamo-enterprise&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow&quot;&gt;Dynamo Enterprise collection&lt;/a&gt; on NGC. These artifacts are eligible for NVIDIA Enterprise Support under an active NVIDIA AI Enterprise subscription and carry no functional or binary differences from their open-source counterparts. See &lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.nvidia.com/dynamo/dev/reference/enterprise/overview&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow&quot;&gt;Dynamo Enterprise&lt;/a&gt; for scope, supported artifacts, and coverage terms.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Looking Ahead&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Planner Runtime Reconfiguration&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Planner reconfigures GPU budgets at runtime through a &lt;code&gt;/v1/min-endpoints&lt;/code&gt; API and caps how many replicas change in one throughput-scaling step, so autoscaling can be steered without a redeploy.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Kubernetes Roles &amp;amp; Standalone Endpoint Picker&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Component roles gain a gated &lt;code&gt;podTemplate&lt;/code&gt; API and explicit per-role replica counts. The Rust Endpoint Picker, now the default inside the Frontend image, continues toward a standalone image, adding an SGLang tokenizer provider and routing runtime requests under the requested policy class.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Frontend Transport Security&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The transport encryption in this release extends to the Frontend HTTP server with mutual TLS.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;</content>
    <author>
      <name>dagil-nvidia</name>
    </author>
    <media:thumbnail height="30" width="30" url="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/221734541?s=60&amp;v=4"/>
  </entry>
  <entry>
    <id>tag:github.com,2008:Repository/942206898/v1.4.1-k-exaone-2.0-750b-post.1</id>
    <updated>2026-09-17T19:53:45Z</updated>
    <link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/releases/tag/v1.4.1-k-exaone-2.0-750b-post.1"/>
    <title>Dynamo v1.4.1-k-exaone-2.0-750b-post.1</title>
    <content type="html">&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Release Notes&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dynamo v1.4.1-k-exaone-2.0-750b-post.1&lt;/strong&gt; is an experimental snapshot build with early &lt;strong&gt;LG AI Research K-EXAONE 2.0&lt;/strong&gt; support on the Dynamo &lt;strong&gt;vLLM&lt;/strong&gt; backend. It is &lt;strong&gt;not recommended for production&lt;/strong&gt; and is not a QA-gated release. APIs, behavior, and defaults may change before stable support. Use it for evaluation, testing, and early feedback only.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Summary&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Dynamo v1.4.1-k-exaone-2.0-750b-post.1 adds serving for &lt;strong&gt;&lt;code&gt;LGAI-EXAONE/K-EXAONE-2.0-750B-A37B-NVFP4&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; on B200 GPUs through Dynamo vLLM 0.28.0. The runtime registers the checkpoint’s &lt;code&gt;ExaoneMoeForCausalLM&lt;/code&gt; architecture and patches &lt;code&gt;exaone_moe&lt;/code&gt; so &lt;code&gt;lm_head&lt;/code&gt; keeps a real module prefix — without that, NVFP4 exclusion rules miss the head and load fails. The Dynamo frontend uses the &lt;code&gt;qwen3&lt;/code&gt; reasoning parser and &lt;code&gt;qwen3_coder&lt;/code&gt; tool-call parser (&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14599&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14599/hovercard&quot;&gt;#14599&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Kubernetes recipes cover a 4-GPU aggregated chat profile (TP4) and an 8-GPU disaggregated 1P1D chat profile (TP4 prefill + TP4 decode, NIXL/UCX KV transfer over InfiniBand RDMA). Both pin &lt;strong&gt;FLASHINFER_CUTLASS&lt;/strong&gt; MoE, MTP (&lt;code&gt;exaone_moe_mtp&lt;/code&gt;, draft length 2), native 262,144 context, KV-aware routing, a shared model-cache PVC/download job, and an AIPerf chat-trace job under &lt;code&gt;recipes/k-exaone-2.0&lt;/code&gt; (&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14822&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14822/hovercard&quot;&gt;#14822&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15016&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15016/hovercard&quot;&gt;#15016&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Base Branch&lt;/strong&gt;: &lt;code&gt;release/1.4.1&lt;/code&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Base Commit&lt;/strong&gt;: &lt;code&gt;2112d6ba74da72e2715ae69f4b76458b7691380d&lt;/code&gt; (2026-08-22)&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Preview Branch&lt;/strong&gt;: &lt;code&gt;release/1.4.1-k-exaone-2.0-750b-post.1&lt;/code&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Preview Tip&lt;/strong&gt;: &lt;code&gt;effab39d4ede05e852d1a4250f711e98fe9e3635&lt;/code&gt; (2026-09-17)&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;vLLM&lt;/strong&gt;: &lt;code&gt;v0.28.0-ubuntu2404&lt;/code&gt; (&lt;code&gt;vllm/vllm-openai&lt;/code&gt;), CUDA 13.0, NIXL v1.3.2 (UCX v1.21.0)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Container Images&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;Backend&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;Arch&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;Image&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;vLLM (CUDA 13)&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;multi-arch (&lt;code&gt;amd64&lt;/code&gt; + &lt;code&gt;arm64&lt;/code&gt;)&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;nvcr.io/nvidia/ai-dynamo/vllm-runtime:1.4.1-k-exaone-2.0-750b-post.1&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Workers use that runtime. Frontends use the released &lt;code&gt;nvcr.io/nvidia/ai-dynamo/dynamo-frontend:1.4.1&lt;/code&gt; image.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Backend Versions&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;Backend&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;Source&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;CUDA&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;Python&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;Notes&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;vLLM&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;Dynamo-built runtime on &lt;code&gt;vllm/vllm-openai:v0.28.0-ubuntu2404&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;13.0&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;3.12&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;NIXL v1.3.2; &lt;code&gt;exaone_moe&lt;/code&gt; &lt;code&gt;lm_head&lt;/code&gt; prefix patch; architecture key &lt;code&gt;ExaoneMoeForCausalLM&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Models&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;Model&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;Precision&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;GPU&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;Notes&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;LGAI-EXAONE/K-EXAONE-2.0-750B-A37B-NVFP4&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;NVFP4 (W4A4) weights, FP8 KV cache&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;B200&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;764.5 B total / ~37 B active, 78 layers (20 full + 58 sliding attention), 256 experts top-8, 262,144 native context; &lt;code&gt;qwen3&lt;/code&gt; / &lt;code&gt;qwen3_coder&lt;/code&gt; parsers; MTP &lt;code&gt;exaone_moe_mtp&lt;/code&gt; DL=2&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About K-EXAONE 2.0&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;K-EXAONE 2.0&lt;/strong&gt; is LG AI Research’s hybrid-attention MoE checkpoint published on Hugging Face as &lt;code&gt;LGAI-EXAONE/K-EXAONE-2.0-750B-A37B-NVFP4&lt;/code&gt; (~530 GB on disk). This build serves it through Dynamo’s vLLM backend on B200, with reasoning, tool calling, MTP, and aggregated or 1P1D disaggregated topologies.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Full Changelog&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;vLLM Backend&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;K-EXAONE architecture on vLLM 0.28.0:&lt;/strong&gt; Bumps the vLLM runtime from 0.26.0 to &lt;code&gt;v0.28.0-ubuntu2404&lt;/code&gt; so the registry key matches the checkpoint’s &lt;code&gt;ExaoneMoeForCausalLM&lt;/code&gt; architecture (&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14599&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14599/hovercard&quot;&gt;#14599&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;NVFP4 &lt;code&gt;lm_head&lt;/code&gt; load:&lt;/strong&gt; Patches &lt;code&gt;exaone_moe&lt;/code&gt; to pass &lt;code&gt;prefix=maybe_prefix(prefix, &quot;lm_head&quot;)&lt;/code&gt; on &lt;code&gt;ParallelLMHead&lt;/code&gt;. Without it, NVFP4 exclusion never matches &lt;code&gt;lm_head&lt;/code&gt; and the unquantized BF16 head fails to load (&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14599&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14599/hovercard&quot;&gt;#14599&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Recipes&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Added K-EXAONE 2.0 deployment recipes:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;code&gt;recipes/k-exaone-2.0&lt;/code&gt; — shared model-cache PVC and Hugging Face download, aggregated TP4 chat on 4× B200, disaggregated 1P1D chat on 8× B200 (&lt;code&gt;NixlConnector&lt;/code&gt; KV transfer over InfiniBand RDMA), mandatory FLASHINFER_CUTLASS MoE, MTP (&lt;code&gt;exaone_moe_mtp&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;--spec-tokens 2&lt;/code&gt;), Dynamo &lt;code&gt;--dyn-reasoning-parser qwen3&lt;/code&gt; / &lt;code&gt;--dyn-tool-call-parser qwen3_coder&lt;/code&gt;, KV-aware routing wired on frontend and workers, startup probes for the long first load, and an AIPerf job on the 8k/1k chat trace (&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/tree/effab39d4ede05e852d1a4250f711e98fe9e3635/recipes/k-exaone-2.0&quot;&gt;recipe folder&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/blob/effab39d4ede05e852d1a4250f711e98fe9e3635/recipes/k-exaone-2.0/README.md&quot;&gt;README&lt;/a&gt;) (&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14822&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14822/hovercard&quot;&gt;#14822&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15016&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/15016/hovercard&quot;&gt;#15016&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Getting Started&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Deployment is Kubernetes-based (Dynamo Platform + &lt;code&gt;DynamoGraphDeployment&lt;/code&gt;). Full steps — namespace, model-cache PVC, Hugging Face download job, DGD apply, &lt;code&gt;/v1/chat/completions&lt;/code&gt; smoke test, and AIPerf — are in the &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/blob/effab39d4ede05e852d1a4250f711e98fe9e3635/recipes/k-exaone-2.0/README.md&quot;&gt;recipe README&lt;/a&gt;. Recipes expect a Hugging Face token secret named &lt;code&gt;hf-token-secret&lt;/code&gt;. First start is 40–120 minutes (53 shards, autotune, CUDA-graph capture).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a reasoning model: smoke tests should use &lt;strong&gt;temperature 0.6 / top_p 0.95&lt;/strong&gt;, a real token budget (&lt;code&gt;max_tokens&lt;/code&gt; well above 256), and read &lt;code&gt;.content // .reasoning_content&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Known Issues / Limitations&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;This is a branch-specific snapshot build, not a QA-gated stable release.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;This release supports the Dynamo vLLM backend on B200 only. Stock Dynamo 1.4.1 vLLM (0.26.0) cannot load this checkpoint.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;code&gt;--kernel-config &#39;{&quot;moe_backend&quot;:&quot;FLASHINFER_CUTLASS&quot;}&#39;&lt;/code&gt; is required. vLLM &lt;code&gt;auto&lt;/code&gt; selects FLASHINFER_TRTLLM and can silently corrupt long-form output on this checkpoint.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;On disaggregated serving, prefill and decode must use the same MTP settings and &lt;code&gt;--block-size 64&lt;/code&gt;. A mismatch changes KV block geometry and produces silent garbage rather than an error.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The disaggregated recipe requests &lt;code&gt;rdma/shared_ib&lt;/code&gt;; set that name to the RDMA resource your cluster actually exposes. Confirm UCX selected InfiniBand (&lt;code&gt;rc_mlx5&lt;/code&gt; / &lt;code&gt;rc&lt;/code&gt;) before trusting TTFT.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Do not add &lt;code&gt;--load-format fastsafetensors&lt;/code&gt; unless GPUDirect Storage is present; without GDS the loader can stall before opening a shard.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;KV-aware routing is wired, but inert at the shipped &lt;code&gt;replicas: 1&lt;/code&gt;. Raising replicas is enough to activate it; on this workload prefix hit rate is already capacity-bound (~8.8%).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;</content>
    <author>
      <name>ynpandey-nv</name>
    </author>
    <media:thumbnail height="30" width="30" url="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20666257?s=60&amp;v=4"/>
  </entry>
  <entry>
    <id>tag:github.com,2008:Repository/942206898/v1.4.1-solar-open2-250b-post.1</id>
    <updated>2026-09-16T02:47:04Z</updated>
    <link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/releases/tag/v1.4.1-solar-open2-250b-post.1"/>
    <title>Dynamo v1.4.1-solar-open2-250b-post.1</title>
    <content type="html">&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Release Notes&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dynamo v1.4.1-solar-open2-250b-post.1&lt;/strong&gt; is an experimental snapshot build with early &lt;strong&gt;Solar Open2 250B&lt;/strong&gt; support on the Dynamo &lt;strong&gt;vLLM&lt;/strong&gt; backend. It is &lt;strong&gt;not recommended for production&lt;/strong&gt; and is not a QA-gated release. APIs, behavior, and defaults may change before stable support. Use it for evaluation, testing, and early feedback only.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Summary&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Dynamo v1.4.1-solar-open2-250b-post.1 adds serving for &lt;strong&gt;&lt;code&gt;nota-ai/Solar-Open2-250B-Nota-NVFP4&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; on B200 GPUs through Dynamo vLLM 0.26.0. The runtime registers the &lt;code&gt;SolarOpen2ForCausalLM&lt;/code&gt; architecture and config, the KDA linear-attention custom op, Solar Open2 reasoning and tool-call parsers, and a chat-template logits processor. The Dynamo frontend keeps special tokens in the stream when a reasoning parser is configured and honors the model&#39;s start-of-tool marker (&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14556&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14556/hovercard&quot;&gt;#14556&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Kubernetes recipes cover a 4-GPU aggregated chat profile (two TP2 replicas, KV-aware routing) and an 8-GPU disaggregated 1P:2D chat profile (one TP4+EP prefill worker and two TP2 decode workers, NIXL/RDMA KV transfer). Both share a revision-pinned model-cache PVC/download job and AIPerf chat-trace jobs under &lt;code&gt;recipes/solar-open2-250b&lt;/code&gt; (&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14912&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14912/hovercard&quot;&gt;#14912&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14376&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14376/hovercard&quot;&gt;#14376&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Base Branch&lt;/strong&gt;: &lt;code&gt;release/1.4.1&lt;/code&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Base Commit&lt;/strong&gt;: &lt;code&gt;2112d6ba74da72e2715ae69f4b76458b7691380d&lt;/code&gt; (2026-08-22)&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Preview Branch&lt;/strong&gt;: &lt;code&gt;release/1.4.1-solar-open2-250b-post.1&lt;/code&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Preview Tip&lt;/strong&gt;: &lt;code&gt;08d7f10f8b6622427d9f0ba900ff3f5e0f904bd2&lt;/code&gt; (2026-09-16)&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;vLLM&lt;/strong&gt;: &lt;code&gt;v0.26.0-ubuntu2404&lt;/code&gt; (&lt;code&gt;vllm/vllm-openai&lt;/code&gt;), CUDA 13.0, NIXL v1.3.2 (UCX v1.21.0)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Container Images&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;Backend&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;Arch&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;Image&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;vLLM (CUDA 13)&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;multi-arch (&lt;code&gt;amd64&lt;/code&gt; + &lt;code&gt;arm64&lt;/code&gt;)&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;nvcr.io/nvidia/ai-dynamo/vllm-runtime:1.4.1-solar-open2-250b-post.1&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Recipes pin that image by digest &lt;code&gt;sha256:42fd3ed0607aa19b7d4c1b0a8f8aaaefefc8ec6292294ea2b5e6757353891f49&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Backend Versions&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;Backend&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;Source&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;CUDA&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;Python&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;Notes&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;vLLM&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;Dynamo-built runtime on &lt;code&gt;vllm/vllm-openai:v0.26.0-ubuntu2404&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;13.0&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;3.12&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;NIXL v1.3.2; Python-only Solar Open2 architecture and parser patches; no custom vLLM kernel build&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Models&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;Model&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;Precision&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;GPU&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;Notes&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;nota-ai/Solar-Open2-250B-Nota-NVFP4&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;NVFP4 weights, FP8 KV cache&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;B200&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;Hybrid GQA + KDA linear attention; 1M context; revision pinned to &lt;code&gt;3cc673335f4c2f41181e05a98fc2b8324d586a64&lt;/code&gt;; &lt;code&gt;solar_open2&lt;/code&gt; reasoning and tool-call parsers&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Solar Open2 250B&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Solar Open2 250B&lt;/strong&gt; is served from the Nota NVFP4 checkpoint on Hugging Face as &lt;code&gt;nota-ai/Solar-Open2-250B-Nota-NVFP4&lt;/code&gt;. This build serves it through Dynamo&#39;s vLLM backend with reasoning and tool calling on B200, in aggregated KV-aware and disaggregated NIXL/RDMA topologies.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Full Changelog&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;vLLM Backend&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Solar Open2 architecture:&lt;/strong&gt; Registers &lt;code&gt;SolarOpen2ForCausalLM&lt;/code&gt; / &lt;code&gt;SolarOpen2Config&lt;/code&gt; and the KDA linear-attention custom op so the hybrid attention graph compiles on vLLM 0.26.0 (&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14556&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14556/hovercard&quot;&gt;#14556&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Reasoning and tool calling:&lt;/strong&gt; Adds the Solar Open2 reasoning parser, tool-call parser, and chat-template logits processor, and hardens shared tool-parser handling when a tool schema &lt;code&gt;properties&lt;/code&gt; field is not a dictionary (&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14556&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14556/hovercard&quot;&gt;#14556&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Frontend compatibility:&lt;/strong&gt; Leaves special tokens in the stream when a reasoning parser is configured, and considers the model&#39;s start-of-tool marker during tool-call lookup (&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14556&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14556/hovercard&quot;&gt;#14556&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build-time validation:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;code&gt;validate_solar_open2_port.py&lt;/code&gt; fails the image build unless the architecture, parsers, and attention op register (&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14556&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14556/hovercard&quot;&gt;#14556&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Recipes&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Added Solar Open2 250B deployment recipes:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;code&gt;recipes/solar-open2-250b&lt;/code&gt; — shared 1200Gi model-cache PVC and revision-pinned Hugging Face download, aggregated 2×TP2 chat on 4× B200 with KV-aware routing, disaggregated 1P:2D chat on 8× B200 (&lt;code&gt;NixlConnector&lt;/code&gt; KV transfer over RDMA/InfiniBand), and AIPerf jobs for the chat trace (&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/tree/08d7f10f8b6622427d9f0ba900ff3f5e0f904bd2/recipes/solar-open2-250b&quot;&gt;recipe folder&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/blob/08d7f10f8b6622427d9f0ba900ff3f5e0f904bd2/docs/fern/pages/recipes/model-recipes/solar-open2-250b.mdx&quot;&gt;docs&lt;/a&gt;) (&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14912&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14912/hovercard&quot;&gt;#14912&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14376&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14376/hovercard&quot;&gt;#14376&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Getting Started&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Deployment is Kubernetes-based (Dynamo Platform + &lt;code&gt;DynamoGraphDeployment&lt;/code&gt;). Full steps — namespace, model-cache PVC, Hugging Face download job, DGD apply, &lt;code&gt;/v1/chat/completions&lt;/code&gt; smoke test, and AIPerf — are in the &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/blob/08d7f10f8b6622427d9f0ba900ff3f5e0f904bd2/docs/fern/pages/recipes/model-recipes/solar-open2-250b.mdx&quot;&gt;recipe docs&lt;/a&gt;. Recipes expect an &lt;code&gt;nvcr.io&lt;/code&gt; image-pull secret and a Hugging Face token secret named &lt;code&gt;hf-token-secret&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Known Issues / Limitations&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;This is a branch-specific snapshot build, not a QA-gated stable release.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;This release supports the Dynamo vLLM backend on B200 only. The stock Dynamo 1.4.1 vLLM runtime cannot load this checkpoint.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Speculative decoding is not supported on this checkpoint and is not enabled.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The disaggregated profile requires &lt;code&gt;VLLM_SSM_CONV_STATE_LAYOUT=DS&lt;/code&gt; and an &lt;code&gt;rdma/ib&lt;/code&gt; (or equivalent) device plugin; without the IB device, KV transfer silently falls back to TCP.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solar Open2 is a reasoning model. Short &lt;code&gt;max_tokens&lt;/code&gt; often truncates mid-reasoning (&lt;code&gt;finish_reason=length&lt;/code&gt;) with an empty &lt;code&gt;content&lt;/code&gt; field; omit &lt;code&gt;max_tokens&lt;/code&gt; or set it well above the reasoning length the workload needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;</content>
    <author>
      <name>ynpandey-nv</name>
    </author>
    <media:thumbnail height="30" width="30" url="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20666257?s=60&amp;v=4"/>
  </entry>
  <entry>
    <id>tag:github.com,2008:Repository/942206898/v1.4.1-a.x-k2-post.1</id>
    <updated>2026-09-15T21:39:06Z</updated>
    <link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/releases/tag/v1.4.1-a.x-k2-post.1"/>
    <title>Dynamo v1.4.1-a.x-k2-post.1</title>
    <content type="html">&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Release Notes&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dynamo v1.4.1-a.x-k2-post.1&lt;/strong&gt; is an experimental snapshot build with early &lt;strong&gt;A.X-K2&lt;/strong&gt; support on the Dynamo &lt;strong&gt;vLLM&lt;/strong&gt; backend. It is &lt;strong&gt;not recommended for production&lt;/strong&gt; and is not a QA-gated release. APIs, behavior, and defaults may change before stable support. Use it for evaluation, testing, and early feedback only.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Summary&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Dynamo v1.4.1-a.x-k2-post.1 adds serving for &lt;strong&gt;&lt;code&gt;skt/A.X-K2-NVFP4&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; on B200 GPUs through Dynamo vLLM 0.26.0. The runtime includes A.X-K2 model and configuration registration, DSpark-compatible speculative-decoding behavior, and KV-cache support for sparse MLA targets with sliding-window draft models.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Kubernetes recipes provide an 8-GPU aggregated deployment and a 12-GPU 2-prefill/1-decode disaggregated deployment. Both use TP4 workers, NVFP4 model weights, FP8 KV cache, KV-aware routing, and revision-pinned EAGLE3 speculative decoding with three speculative tokens. The disaggregated profile transfers KV state through NIXL over UCX.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Release Branch&lt;/strong&gt;: &lt;code&gt;release/1.4.1-a.x-k2-post.1&lt;/code&gt;, tip &lt;code&gt;020c9905910df391f3eb206d06b727937aa17a92&lt;/code&gt; (2026-09-15)&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;vLLM&lt;/strong&gt;: &lt;code&gt;0.26.0&lt;/code&gt; with A.X-K2 patches 0001–0004&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Container Images&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;Backend&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;Arch&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;Image&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;vLLM&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;multi-arch (&lt;code&gt;amd64&lt;/code&gt; + &lt;code&gt;arm64&lt;/code&gt;)&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;nvcr.io/nvidia/ai-dynamo/vllm-runtime:1.4.1-a.x-k2-post.1&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Backend Versions&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;Backend&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;Source&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;Notes&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;vLLM&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;Dynamo v1.4.1 runtime with vLLM 0.26.0&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;A.X-K2 model/config support, DSpark anchor-sampling layout, and sparse-MLA KV-cache compatibility&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Models&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;Model&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;Precision&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;GPU&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;Notes&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;skt/A.X-K2-NVFP4&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;NVFP4 weights, FP8 KV cache&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;B200&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;Target model; revision pinned to &lt;code&gt;9e2e804e80f8d1b3afba5d7938173cec1ed46b49&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;skt/A.X-K2-EAGLE3&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;EAGLE3 draft model&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;B200&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;Three speculative tokens; revision pinned to &lt;code&gt;24958e91737d760908f73a8af4b6e06080fc5c1d&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About A.X-K2&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A.X-K2&lt;/strong&gt; is served with NVFP4 weights and FP8 KV cache on B200 GPUs. This build supports aggregated and disaggregated Dynamo deployments, KV-aware routing, and EAGLE3 speculative decoding. The disaggregated profile separates prefill and decode workers while transferring KV state over NIXL/UCX.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Full Changelog&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;vLLM Backend&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A.X-K2 model support:&lt;/strong&gt; Adds the A.X-K2 model and configuration to the Dynamo vLLM runtime and rejects unsupported checkpoints that use non-fused attention gates.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Speculative decoding:&lt;/strong&gt; Honors the DSpark anchor-sampling layout used by A.X-K2 speculative decoding.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;KV-cache compatibility:&lt;/strong&gt; Supports sparse MLA target models paired with sliding-window draft models.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build-time validation:&lt;/strong&gt; Validates model registration, DSpark integration, and KV-cache wiring while building the runtime.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Container change:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14554&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14554/hovercard&quot;&gt;PR #14554&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Recipes&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Aggregated serving:&lt;/strong&gt; Two TP4 workers across 8 B200 GPUs with KV-aware routing, NVFP4 weights, FP8 KV cache, and EAGLE3 speculative decoding.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Disaggregated serving:&lt;/strong&gt; Two TP4 prefill workers and one TP4 decode worker across 12 B200 GPUs, with KV-aware routing and NIXL/UCX KV transfer.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Model caching:&lt;/strong&gt; Shared PVC and revision-pinned download job for the target and EAGLE3 draft models.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benchmarking:&lt;/strong&gt; AIPerf 0.12.0 workflow for a Mooncake chat trace with 8K input, 1K output, 70% KV reuse, and concurrency 16. An optional synthetic EAGLE3 acceptance-length profile (&lt;code&gt;AL=2.12&lt;/code&gt;) is provided for throughput-only measurements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Recipe change:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14635&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14635/hovercard&quot;&gt;PR #14635&lt;/a&gt;, included on this release branch by &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14883&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14883/hovercard&quot;&gt;PR #14883&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Getting Started&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Deployment is Kubernetes-based using the Dynamo Platform and &lt;code&gt;DynamoGraphDeployment&lt;/code&gt;. The &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/tree/020c9905910df391f3eb206d06b727937aa17a92/recipes/ax-k2&quot;&gt;A.X-K2 recipe&lt;/a&gt; includes model-cache setup, aggregated and disaggregated manifests, deployment instructions, smoke-test guidance, and the AIPerf benchmark workflow. Recipes expect an &lt;code&gt;nvcr.io&lt;/code&gt; image-pull secret and a Hugging Face token secret named &lt;code&gt;hf-token-secret&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Known Issues / Limitations&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experimental snapshot build — not QA-gated and not recommended for production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;This release supports the Dynamo vLLM backend only.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deployment recipes target B200 GPUs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The synthetic EAGLE3 acceptance profile is intended only for throughput benchmarking, not functional or quality validation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Published benchmark results predate the final published NVCR runtime image and should not be treated as measurements of this exact build.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The recorded disaggregated benchmark completed 1,755 of 1,765 requests; ten requests failed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;</content>
    <author>
      <name>ynpandey-nv</name>
    </author>
    <media:thumbnail height="30" width="30" url="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20666257?s=60&amp;v=4"/>
  </entry>
  <entry>
    <id>tag:github.com,2008:Repository/942206898/v1.6.0-deepseek-v4.1-flash-dev.1</id>
    <updated>2026-09-12T02:33:02Z</updated>
    <link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/releases/tag/v1.6.0-deepseek-v4.1-flash-dev.1"/>
    <title>Dynamo v1.6.0-deepseek-v4.1-flash-dev.1</title>
    <content type="html">&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Release Notes&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dynamo v1.6.0-deepseek-v4.1-flash-dev.1&lt;/strong&gt; is an experimental snapshot build with early &lt;strong&gt;DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash&lt;/strong&gt; support on the Dynamo &lt;strong&gt;SGLang&lt;/strong&gt; backend. It is &lt;strong&gt;not recommended for production&lt;/strong&gt; and is not a QA-gated release. APIs, behavior, and defaults may change before stable support. Use it for evaluation, testing, and early feedback only.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Summary&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Dynamo v1.6.0-deepseek-v4.1-flash-dev.1 adds serving for &lt;strong&gt;&lt;code&gt;deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; on Dynamo &lt;strong&gt;SGLang&lt;/strong&gt;. The published container is built on the CUDA 13 SGLang &lt;code&gt;dev-dsv41&lt;/code&gt; preview base and includes native DeepSeek V4.1 frontend support: Rust prompt rendering, automatic &lt;code&gt;deepseek_v41&lt;/code&gt; reasoning and tool-call parsing, streamed DSML handling, and rejection of completed malformed tool-call arguments (&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14690&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14690/hovercard&quot;&gt;#14690&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Kubernetes recipes cover 8x GB200 aggregated (two TP4/EP4 workers, KV-aware routing, DSpark speculative decoding) and 1P1D disaggregated (TP4/EP4 per role, Mooncake KV transfer over TCP or GKE RDMA) profiles, plus a shared model-cache PVC and Hugging Face download job pinned to revision &lt;code&gt;dba1be0a40aa45a94ad051997016db3960a90277&lt;/code&gt;. Both targets serve up to 1,048,576 tokens of context. Neither target is benchmarked (&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14682&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14682/hovercard&quot;&gt;#14682&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14763&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14763/hovercard&quot;&gt;#14763&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Release Branch&lt;/strong&gt;: &lt;code&gt;release/1.6.0-deepseek-v4.1-flash-dev.1&lt;/code&gt;, tip &lt;code&gt;7931147d403c554575438c2451da4248e53e10b8&lt;/code&gt; (2026-09-12)&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;SGLang&lt;/strong&gt;: &lt;code&gt;lmsysorg/sglang:dev-dsv41@sha256:e56358a68b06427362283c8c8a9d7d706448082ae53098ea1131b5d51aa1fd62&lt;/code&gt; (CUDA 13), NIXL v1.4.0&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Container Images&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;Backend&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;Arch&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;Image&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;SGLang (CUDA 13)&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;multi-arch (&lt;code&gt;amd64&lt;/code&gt; + &lt;code&gt;arm64&lt;/code&gt;)&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;nvcr.io/nvidia/ai-dynamo/sglang-runtime:1.6.0-deepseek-v4.1-flash-dev.1&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Backend Versions&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;Backend&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;Source&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;CUDA&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;Python&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;Notes&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;SGLang&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;Dynamo-built runtime on &lt;code&gt;lmsysorg/sglang:dev-dsv41&lt;/code&gt; (digest-pinned), with non-runtime packages pruned from the upstream development image&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;13.0&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;3.12&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;NIXL v1.4.0; DeepSeek V4.1 has not shipped in a numbered SGLang release yet&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Models&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;Model&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;Precision&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;GPU&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;Notes&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;FP8 dense, FP4 MoE experts, FP8 KV (&lt;code&gt;fp8_e4m3&lt;/code&gt;)&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;8x GB200&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td align=&quot;left&quot;&gt;SGLang &lt;code&gt;dev-dsv41&lt;/code&gt;; aggregated TP4/EP4 (DSpark k=5, KV-aware routing) or 1P1D disagg TP4/EP4 per role (no speculation); 1M context; &lt;code&gt;deepseek_v41&lt;/code&gt; reasoning and tool-call parsers&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash is a Mixture-of-Experts checkpoint from DeepSeek (&lt;code&gt;deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash&lt;/code&gt;; about 510 GB). Routed experts ship FP4, dense weights are FP8, and the engine uses an FP8 KV cache. This preview serves the full 1,048,576-token window on GB200 through Dynamo&#39;s SGLang backend, with reasoning, tool calling, streaming chat, and schema-constrained output. The checkpoint also accepts images; the recipes in this build serve text only.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Full Changelog&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SGLang Backend&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;DeepSeek V4.1 frontend:&lt;/strong&gt; Native Rust prompt rendering and unified reasoning/tool-call parsing for DeepSeek V4.1, including automatic parser selection from model metadata, preserved partial DSML markers across streamed chunks, normalized reasoning-effort values, and rejection of completed malformed DSML arguments during batch aggregation (&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14690&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14690/hovercard&quot;&gt;#14690&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SGLang &lt;code&gt;dev-dsv41&lt;/code&gt; runtime:&lt;/strong&gt; Pins the CUDA 13 SGLang runtime to the digest-pinned &lt;code&gt;lmsysorg/sglang:dev-dsv41&lt;/code&gt; preview base required to serve this model, and trims non-runtime packages from that development image (&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14690&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14690/hovercard&quot;&gt;#14690&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Recipes&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash SGLang GB200 recipes:&lt;/strong&gt; Added &lt;code&gt;recipes/deepseek-v4.1-flash&lt;/code&gt; — shared model-cache PVC/download job (pinned HF revision), aggregated GB200 (&lt;code&gt;sglang/agg-gb200&lt;/code&gt;: two TP4 workers, KV-aware routing, DSpark block size 5, decode CUDA-graph batch capped at 64), and disaggregated GB200 1P1D (&lt;code&gt;sglang/disagg-gb200&lt;/code&gt;: generic Mooncake TCP target plus GKE RDMA variant). Both profiles use &lt;code&gt;sglang-runtime:1.6.0-deepseek-v4.1-flash-dev.1&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;deepseek_v41&lt;/code&gt; parsers, and 1M context. Day-0 functional scope only; no published performance claim (&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/tree/7931147d403c554575438c2451da4248e53e10b8/recipes/deepseek-v4.1-flash&quot;&gt;recipe folder&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/blob/7931147d403c554575438c2451da4248e53e10b8/recipes/deepseek-v4.1-flash/README.md&quot;&gt;README&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.nvidia.com/dynamo/dev/recipes/deepseek-v4-1-flash&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow&quot;&gt;docs&lt;/a&gt;) (&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14682&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14682/hovercard&quot;&gt;#14682&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14763&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/14763/hovercard&quot;&gt;#14763&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Getting Started&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Deployment is Kubernetes-based (Dynamo Platform + &lt;code&gt;DynamoGraphDeployment&lt;/code&gt;). Full steps — namespace, Hugging Face token, model-cache PVC, download job, DGD apply, and a &lt;code&gt;/v1/chat/completions&lt;/code&gt; smoke test — are in the &lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.nvidia.com/dynamo/dev/recipes/deepseek-v4-1-flash&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow&quot;&gt;recipe docs&lt;/a&gt; and the &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/blob/7931147d403c554575438c2451da4248e53e10b8/recipes/deepseek-v4.1-flash/README.md&quot;&gt;recipe README&lt;/a&gt;. Recipes expect an &lt;code&gt;nvcr.io&lt;/code&gt; image-pull secret and a Hugging Face token secret named &lt;code&gt;hf-token-secret&lt;/code&gt; with access to &lt;code&gt;deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash&lt;/code&gt;. GB200 recipes require ARM-node scheduling (two nodes, 4 GPUs each).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Read the smoke-test response body, not only the HTTP status. On the disaggregated target a KV transfer failure can still return HTTP 200 with &lt;code&gt;content: null&lt;/code&gt; and zero completion tokens.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Known Issues / Limitations&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;This is a branch-specific snapshot build, not a QA-gated stable release.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Day-0 recipes only: both targets passed a functional probe; neither is benchmarked.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Disaggregated SGLang does not support DSpark for this model. Use the aggregated target for speculative decoding.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generic disaggregated KV is pinned to Mooncake TCP (&lt;code&gt;MC_FORCE_TCP=1&lt;/code&gt;). The GKE variant uses RDMA and DMA-BUF (&lt;code&gt;WITH_NVIDIA_PEERMEM=0&lt;/code&gt;). The NVLink fabric is faster but needs both workers in one NVLink clique; a split placement reports Ready and returns empty completions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;KV-aware routing is a no-op on the disaggregated target with a single decode worker.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Recipes serve text only, even though the checkpoint accepts images.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Both targets set &lt;code&gt;SGLANG_DEFAULT_THINKING=true&lt;/code&gt;. Thinking is off by default for this model, and then &lt;code&gt;reasoning_content&lt;/code&gt; is empty.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;GB200 recipes require ARM-node scheduling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;</content>
